{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/442841-ooc-werewolf-2nd-ed-pbp-ooc-prep-with-dusksage-co","id":442841,"title":"[OOC] Werewolf 2nd Ed PBP OOC Prep with Dusksage & Co","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play","Play by Post"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-15T11:18:37-07:00","id":442841,"title":"[OOC] Werewolf 2nd Ed PBP OOC Prep with Dusksage & Co","content":"This is the OOC room for the game started here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/429607-looking-for-group-w-tf2-just-came-out-guys-how-big-of-a-deal-is-this-eh-eh\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/g...-is-this-eh-eh</a> game's full, we're just chatting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T11:42:00-07:00","id":442864,"title":"","content":"Aliza Carter is a Bone Shadow Cahalith who is all about being a font of knowledge and direction for her pack. She may not be the Alpha, but she'll still be the mother, telling her tales and delving into darkness to find the truths she can return to them to help grant direction and strength. She has deep and abiding respect for the unity of pack and the various roles and burdens her brethren must carry, but her strength is also her weakness -- if her pack is fractured and cannot share its responsibilities, she will reach too far, and too quickly, taking the weight upon herself, collapsing and dragging the others along with her as she falls apart under the strain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3070,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","user":"Barbrarilen","date":". 03-15-2015, 03:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T12:33:06-07:00","id":442961,"title":"","content":"Here would be my concept, planning on a Cahalith Blood Talon, so without further ado, my backstory.<br /> <br /> Simon is an event organiser with a focus on the musical scene and in community integration, seeing the division between different racial and social groups as key to many current issues and tensions. He's a vibrant, focused man, but has little subtlety and his actions are extremely good at being noticed and having an overt response.<br /> <br /> Politically speaking, he has a few low level connections, though a number of people in office find him a nuisance and sometimes even a threat. That would be his human side.<br /> <br /> As a werewolf and a hunter of the Blood Talon tribe, he's even more loud and noisy. His targets tend to end up dead in very brutal, very visible ways and have a tendency to end up in the papers, which is just how he likes it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T16:50:35-07:00","id":443279,"title":"","content":"Very nice start guys, <br /> <br /> This brings our Pack to two Cahalith's, one Blood Talon and one Bone Shadow, and two Irraka, one Iron Master and one Storm Lord. It's looking more and more like this will take place in a city so keep that in mind when choosing your merits and designing your Pack's totem. Also it's certain that this is going to be a mixed Pack so keep in mind which of the Tribes will have the majority since that will determine which prey will be more often called on for Siskur-Dah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Updated 03-15-2015, 08:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T18:36:35-07:00","id":443503,"title":"","content":"Just gonna go ahead and add that my character is an Ithaeur Bone Shadow, little backstory blurb to follow soon.<br /> <br /> Joseph is a werewolf who devotes himself to his study of the Shadow and as one who is called by Luna to know the spirits. Beyond this work however the Uratha has found himself adrift in the werewolf community like the flotsam of his old coastal home. Already he has shifted between three separate packs, each one unable to take the place as his family. To him this is only a natural process that will take time, something that is inevitable as he tries to find his place and not a result of any true failing on his part or that of his former packmates.<br /> <br /> He is nonetheless devoted to each pack he becomes a part of, preferring to resort to claw and fang when managing the Hisil only when binding and negotiating with a spirit have already failed. Like many of his tribe Joseph places a high value on the knowledge spirits possess, seeing acquiring it as more important than outright destroying prey. He must grasp what he can about the spirits that his packmates cannot, and if that means calling out their behavior as unwise and foolish than so be it.<br /> <br /> Before his First Change Joseph grew up in an adopted family. He and his new sister had some talent at singing and at the urging of their parents began performing and as they grew into their mid-teens were even picked up by a small record company. They were never popular outside a small amount of followers in the musical community, performing ballads mostly with a few accompanying instruments. The piano and occasional guitar featured most often and they kept around what could be considered the folk genre of music. Joseph knows he was not the only one to change, but in the chaos of that night he lost his sister and has yet to see her. What he does know however is that the territory where he first changed was hotly contested by the Forsaken and Pure. He knows very well he couldn't draw his claws against his own sibling, but whether or not he would receive the same curtesy is a fear that is always on his heels.<br /> <br /> (This is feeling pretty cardboard/stereotypical to me right now. I've just got done working so I'm a bit burned out and that might be why. Will likely revisit this later).<br /> <br /> (By the by, whats our current feel on the state of the pack? Have we known each other? Are we new? How long have all of us been Uratha? Is this meant to be soon after First Change? etc.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1705,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","user":"Okami","date":". 03-16-2015, 12:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T20:42:23-07:00","id":443694,"title":"","content":"Nice! Looks like Bone Shadows are pulling into the lead by one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T23:29:56-07:00","id":443818,"title":"","content":"To answer your question Okami this pack is indeed new but the Uratha in this Troupe are at least one year after their First Change. They can be Uratha for longer if you want to play more knowledgable Werewolves but I wanted to leave a minimum option for those who do want to play shortly after their first Change. <br /> <br /> As for Pack feel this Pack is newly formed so the group will have known each other for at least several months and share at least one common goal/aspiration. This is also going to be the largest Pack in the city in recent memory among the Forsaken and as such will be kept a close eye on by your fellow Werewolves and possibly others...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T23:38:07-07:00","id":443822,"title":"","content":"Amravanti: My irraka is going to be more of a scout/spy. If your concept was playing up the assassin nature of the auspice there probably won't be much overlap between us, especially with different tribes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Vi is more of a social character and thanks to her job has connections all over the city from drug dealers to local business owners to secrataries and security guards. She's not angry by nature, so the rage that's become an intergral part of herbeing since her change is something she constantly struggles with.<br /> <br /> I'd personally like the pack to be less than a year old and still feeling out their territory, Violet herself is only about a year and a half out from her First Change.<br /> <br /> Are we making wolf blooded and human packmates as well? Any specific questions you want us to answer in our backstory?<br /> <br /> <br /> Here's my initial concept from the recruiting thread, this will be fleshed out more as we hammer down the details:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>soonmot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/429607-looking-for-group-w-tf2-just-came-out-guys-how-big-of-a-deal-is-this-eh-eh?p=442840#post442840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a quick flavor post for the character I've decided on. I'm holding off on a full background until we find out what Dusk wants us to include and if this type of of character is appropriate to the game setting.<br /> Violet Caravell Iron Master Irraka<br /> <br /> \u201cJust cut through the alley between the Starbucks and the artisanal candle store, ride down the stairs and hang a left at the fountain sculpture. You'll beat any car by five minutes. Guaranteed.\u201d<br /> <br /> Violet is part of the city. Her bicycle streaks through the streets and alleys like a half glimpsed ghost as she navigates shortcuts that even longtime residents are unaware of. Her face is known by the secretaries of small local offices and the security desks of huge office buildings and multinationals as she delivers packages from on to another. Even in her free time she travels the city, running, climbing, exploring, and watching. She's seen weird things before, things she convinced herself were perfectly normal but then the Change came on a night with no moon.<br /> <br /> Now her urban exploration has taken on a new urgency. She looks out for the weird. She knows that the pale people who receive night time packages through the service she works for probably aren't human. But neither is she. As fun as biking through the city was, as exciting as running through could be, neither compares to the thrill of racing through the shadows on four legs.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/FfP3jl0.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5337-soonmot","name":"soonmot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5337_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T23:47:23-07:00","id":443827,"title":"","content":"That's the general idea at least. With luck and skill the Pack will hopefully come into their territory by the end of the Chronicle. <br /> <br /> I also have no problem with your concept, live the city flavor so much that it helped me with my city design a little. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In regards to the wolf blooded and mortals/supernatural Packmates I'm willing to have each character make one to two NPC's to add to the pack. Cannot have more Wolf Blooded than the Werewolf number +2. Supernaturals need to be oked bye first and mortals are unlimited. <br /> <br /> I'm currently working on the lay of the land right now so by tomorrow I'm hoping to have a more clearer picture of where this is going to be taking place. Thanks everyone who have such rich back stories, that will reflect the region this Chronicle will take place in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T03:03:46-07:00","id":443970,"title":"","content":"I'll write a full background once I have the time, of course, but I've revised the tribe. She's now a Hunter in Darkness Irraka. I've wanted to make an Irraka for a while do why not go all the way with it. Here's a quick idea before I go to bed. Her name is Indiana (Indy).<br /> <br /> &quot;There's an urban legend around these parts. They call her the Ghost of Stowe Bridge. Some kid was the first to see it. He was tagging the wall behind the old church when he felt it sneak up on him. He couldn't see it, of course, but he could feel it. Just out of sight. Circling him. He felt it drawing nearer and nearer. And then it spoke. It was a young girl's voice. Hearing her speak was like being dropped in a bucket of ice. All it said was &quot;run.&quot; So he did. He hightailed it out of there, but the thing followed him for two whole blocks until he made it home. He locked the door and the he looked out the window onto the street and he saw it. Two yellow eyes staring in at him. He swears it was just the eyes. There was no body. Just the eyes. They blinked once and then they were gone. He doesn't go out much anymore. Neither do I.&quot;<br /> <br /> Well, that ghost is Indy. She's not much for words since the change. If you want to protect the things you love from the things that want to destroy them, you have to move faster than they do. You have to be stronger. She spends most her free time padding through the city in urhan, weaving through back alleys and broken fences. It's all probably a bit reckless, considering there's bound to be more than a few calls to animal control if she's ever spotted. She hasn't been yet, though. The truth is, she feels more like herself on four feet than she ever did in sneakers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T04:48:23-07:00","id":444038,"title":"","content":"There's a saying among librarians, that 'three moves is a fire' - that is to say, if you have to keep moving and shifting and unpacking the stuff you try to keep in order, you are going to wind up with a whole lot of it being destroyed by good intentions.<br /> <br /> Aliza was pretty sure that saying should apply to people as well. She was in her second year of school trying to get her Master's to be a librarian, in her third apartment since she had started, looking for a fourth nearby temp job to help the bills since setting out.<br /> <br /> Bad luck just kept on following her now. The things she saw in dark corners were bad enough, but these days it was like the weird shapes and ghosts were noticing her. And when things started noticing, things started breaking. Water mains, contracts, favorite professors' backs when they slipped on ice. And then classes were canceled and Aliza started to work on transferring credits again.<br /> <br /> When the hallucinations progressed to nightmares - of black pools and hot flesh and frantic chasing and the taste of blood in her mouth - Aliza figured that the fire had happened, and one extra move or change was just one too many. That third apartment never had a chance as her first howl shattered glass and stone and plaster while she savaged the dozens of spirits of misfortune that had settled around her, scattering them to the winds.<br /> <br /> At least now she can name her problems. Describe them and laugh at them and make them an easy pill to swallow so others learn from her mistake. She wanted to be a librarian to help guide other people to what they needed to know. Now she listens to the Moon and the whispers in the shadows, and does the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3070,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","user":"Barbrarilen","date":". 03-16-2015, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T08:14:48-07:00","id":444288,"title":"","content":"So, in terms of merits I'm assuming we're only dealing with those available in 2e core? I imagine the adjustment to GMC would be difficult for some, though I admit I will be sad to see aspects (Totem-Bound is too cool) go. Also speaking of totem's where do we see our new pack in that respect? Do we have a totem or will our first Siskur-Dah be chasing one down through the spirit wilds? What kind of totem do we think we want in the pack? Should we roleplay that out through the characters to figure it out (that actually sounds pretty fun)? Finally, what's our packs territory like? I'm for the urban setting so I think we've definitely settled there. Knowing this will help with the totem a bit I feel since characters would want one that can relate to their place, especially with the Irraka. So, (I know I'm full of questions, please bear with me :/) First, what kind of city do we live in? Is it growing, shrinking, or stagnant? In good times, bad times, perhaps holding its own against recent downturns but more than one threat, spiritually and otherwise are weakening these walls?<br /> <br /> With the larger picture out of the way, whats our specific territory like? Is it in the bad part of town? Did its former pack recently die? Has it been unclaimed thus far? Is it in the art's district? Maybe it contains the cities old park, which could be your usual artificial nature setup or, due to a number of 'activist' groups be a bit larger and more wild than your usual park, even a copse of real trees here and there. Maybe one edge runs along the old tracks no longer in use, letting the old ravine and ecosystem come back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1705,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","user":"Okami","date":". 03-16-2015, 11:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T08:19:12-07:00","id":444293,"title":"","content":"/\\/\\/\\/\\I'm good with either already having one or going out in search of one.<br /> <br /> Beginning of character sheet here: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B-UkBhXlxCQZTlE3NlZNWUFSdWc/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B-U...ew?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> First Change: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B-UkBhXlxCQZSDdPZXo3al81LXc/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B-U...ew?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> Violet's Background: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B-UkBhXlxCQZR0pUcE9CbFV5ODg/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B-U...ew?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> Contacts are gangs and gatekeepers (basically the front desk/ secretaries/ security guards that she interacts with when delivering packages), werewolves (she passes through the territory of many packs in the course of her job and has at least introduced herself), and cyclists<br /> <br /> Grace Whitman, Wolf-Blooded: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B-UkBhXlxCQZSjlOdUJCM1F3dms/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B-U...ew?usp=sharing</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B-UkBhXlxCQZcHV4VldKTHVFd3c/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B-U...ew?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> Derek Pope, human pack member. Snoop and messenger: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B-UkBhXlxCQZS1ltNk1USktGeEE/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B-U...ew?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> Ally is Devon Holt, he's a vampire that can turn into a wolf! Ally might even be too strong a word. Friendly rival? Frenemy? Basically Violet and Devon got into an altercation, he turned into a wolf to flee and she did the same. Now they meet up every now and again and race as wolves through the city before gossiping about weird bullshit. I'll actually be writing a about their first meet up. <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B-UkBhXlxCQZeW1pYmxpVE5QVTQ/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B-U...ew?usp=sharing</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5337,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5337-soonmot","user":"soonmot","date":". 03-25-2015, 12:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5337-soonmot","name":"soonmot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5337_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T08:43:51-07:00","id":444312,"title":"","content":"I would love to hunt our totem. Totems are cool. :-D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T09:18:35-07:00","id":444371,"title":"","content":"I'm liking the notion of hunting one as well, that said when it comes to deciding on what one we want do we want to hash that out in character? Though I'd prefer to know a little bit about the setting first for that. Also, as I'm digging into the nuts and bolts of character creation I have to ask (yet again). Do we as a group want some kind of 'soft cap' on skills at character creation? It states of course you cant raise above five, but five dots is also a form of mastery, which feels weird to me with any 'newish' character (plus when one thinks about going that hard makes a character much less versatile but thats another side to it). Anyway, are we as a group ok with four and five dots in something at character creation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T09:30:43-07:00","id":444397,"title":"","content":"Edited in first change story. Skill wise, I always asked for in world reason a character had a four or five in a skill (with the exception of any free template dot) when I ST. Let's see what our characters are like and start planning out relationships, I'm sure the proper sort of totem will grow from those conversations. I kind of see Barbrarilen's character as the one responsible for forming the pack, probably with Retias help, unless his character joined later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5337-soonmot","name":"soonmot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5337_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T09:36:30-07:00","id":444403,"title":"","content":"I have one skill (thanks free auspice dot) and one attribute at 4 on my character sheet as it stand right now, but if the group decides on a soft cap of 3 I am okay with that. Also, I would love to hunt a totem as I've actually never done that in any of the games I've played. We've always been relatively established.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 03-16-2015, 12:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T10:42:51-07:00","id":444531,"title":"","content":"I don't see a reason to censor what is possible at chargen. If a player will only feel they are pulling their weight with an all-out nine dot brawl+strength dice pool then we shouldn't limit them.<br /> <br /> Also I am happy to have characters connect to Aliza for roots. I kept my post-change limited for now for just that reason ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T10:52:22-07:00","id":444539,"title":"","content":"I like the thought of our totem being an in game thing to acquire, gives u something to really start off with.<br /> <br /> Does anyone mind if I switch to Rahu? That's an auspice we haven't gotten hold of yet. Truth be told, I'm considering working another concept up, since I'm not sure my current one fits too ell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T11:08:33-07:00","id":444565,"title":"","content":"/\\/\\/\\ go for it! I liked your promoter concept, but whatever you'll have the most fun with is the correct answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5337-soonmot","name":"soonmot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5337_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T11:12:41-07:00","id":444569,"title":"","content":"I'd say go for changing if you like, Hmm, part of me agrees with barb that we shouldnt limit it, but as new(ish) uratha I feel a softcap is more accurate to the setting and more in-caharcter. I'll go whichever way the ST and group majority go for the softcap issue. As for when my character joins the pack I see him as a later addition, possibly the last.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T11:35:52-07:00","id":444627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>soonmot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/442841-ooc-werewolf-2nd-ed-pbp-ooc-prep-with-dusksage-co?p=444397#post444397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edited in first change story. Skill wise, I always asked for in world reason a character had a four or five in a skill (with the exception of any free template dot) when I ST. Let's see what our characters are like and start planning out relationships, I'm sure the proper sort of totem will grow from those conversations. I kind of see Barbrarilen's character as the one responsible for forming the pack, probably with Retias help, unless his character joined later.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So, after looking at those lovely pdf's in google doc I gotta ask how you did that, is the character sheet an interactive one from gone? and how does that whole googledoc thing work? Tis a mystery to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T12:34:16-07:00","id":444742,"title":"","content":"This is a character concept I never got to run with, as the game folded before it got going. That said, I'm not completely sure it'd work here. The game was set in California and the research I did was into the Atsugewi tribe. Still, I think the core of it can work, and I'll present it here. He'd be a Rahu Hunter in Darkness.<br /> <br /> Appearance<br /> <br /> Aside from facial features that show his family's native origins, Akule doesn't tend to stand out in a crowd for the most part, preferring casual and reliable clothes that can manage a good amount of wear and tear. His hair is cropped short with a suggestion that he does it himself in front of a mirror, and has little caring for the rather uneven results. <br /> <br /> Personality<br /> <br /> Akule has been a rather defensive, often quite hostile young man since his First Change and the resulting death of a family member. While he's far from incapable of interacting with others, he's fairly wary of it and tends to keep it as limited as he can, with his current lack of trust in himself.<br /> <br /> What it has done is to harden his nature, though also provided the more positive merit of seeing him care about others he sees at risk, a desire to see some good be done closely tied to that.<br /> <br /> Background<br /> <br /> Akule isn't sure whether or not his name fully matches the history of the Atsugewi tribe, but neither are his parents. However, in a small hint of cultural rebellion they settled on a name for him that didn't have such strong Anglican roots and made him stand out more. At times he enjoyed this, but at others, he found frustration at being put in a position that made him stand out. Still, that was far from his biggest issue.<br /> <br /> Spirits do not at all like the wolfblooded and Akule was tormented throughout his childhood by unseen forces that were a puzzle and concern both for him, and the community he grew up in. Ceremonies he took part in were disrupted in small, apparently petty ways and a number of his efforts to connect with others both inside and outside of his local, small community also tended to end badly, to the point where certain, mean spirited others began calling him 'Runs-with-Coyote' behind his back. This did not at all improve his moods as he grew older.<br /> <br /> Born and raised in &lt;City&gt;, he wound up in a number of incidents as he grew older, culminating in a series of rough fights that got him a sharp warning from both his own elders and the police that interrupted the street based tussle. Sixteen, that time he managed to avoid juvenile court, with a warning he would be unlikely to have that luck next time. In an effort to work out some of his tension, his uncle started to take him on camping trips during the holiday periods with other youth who had an interest in exploring historical practices. They hunted, explored and listened to stories in a refreshing break from the mundane nature of day to day life.<br /> <br /> Until four years later, where Akule's uncle died.<br /> <br /> Akule only has scattered memories of the time, but it's enough for him to know what truly happened there. He and Jonas had been tracking a deer, the man having decided to use it as an excuse to try and get to the bottom of his nephew's recent, excessive mood swings. However, the second an arrow pierced the deer's side and spilled blood on the earth, Akule saw red.<br /> <br /> He remembers his uncle screaming for mercy, the blood on his claws and the red, ugly rage. Finer details escape him, but when it was over, Jonas was very much dead and Akule was huddled on the ground in a naked, bloody, weeping heap. The others concluded the two of them had been attacked by a dangerous predator, and Akule's garbled account of events was put down to the harrowing of his experience and witnessing his uncle's death. Aware of the far worse truth, Akule almost immediately left his family and friends behind and retreated into his own place in the city, cutting off contact with his previous life and taking up a low paying job as a butcher.<br /> <br /> It was in that self imposed exile that others of the Forsaken would find him.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T18:59:57-07:00","id":445176,"title":"","content":"Oh, it warms my heart so much to see the collaboration going on in this forum. T ^ T<br /> <br /> Let's get a Uratha roll call so we can get a larger picture of the Pack.<br /> <br /> Also since it looks like there a majortiy consensus already and because the idea is freak'n awesome I would LOVE to have your guy's first Siskur-Dah be to acquire your Pack Totem. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'll also be posting up the setting in a tidbit, but here are the general ideas:<br /> <br /> &gt; Fictional City: Victory City Washington (Costal City)<br /> &gt; Tribe: Shared (Forsaken and Pure tribes are currently at a shakey peace after both faction lost one or more Packs in a Beshilu infestation that occured three years ago.)<br /> &gt; Forsaken Tribes: Root Walkers (Hunters in Darkness who's territory is the entire cities sewers), Whisper Catchers (Bone Shadows who's territory is the Victory City College campus), Half-Light Studios (Mixed Pack that claims the artsy Docktown District as their own), Behemoth's Wake (Another of the mixed Packs that stylizes itself as a nomadic Pack that rides the central highway and keeps it clear of rabble), Knights of Avalon (A Ghost Wolf Pack that protects the Avalon Gated Community after a great tradgedy befell the place), and the Troupe's new Pack.<br /> &gt; Pure Tribes: ??? (You're Packs new so you'll have to discover them for yourself. You'll just know that: Lakehights District, Victory City National Park, and the Projects are Pure territory.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Cleaning up. 03-16-2015, 11:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T20:51:00-07:00","id":445297,"title":"","content":"Big city. O_O Are you sure this isn't just Seattle? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Uratha Role Call!<br /> <br /> Name: Aliza Carter<br /> Tribe: Bone Shadows<br /> Auspice: Gibbous Moon<br /> RP Role: Pack Mother<br /> Hunt Role: Personal/Spiritual Guidance/Direction -- not tactics, but maybe part of the larger 'strategy', the bigger picture<br /> Combat Role: ?? (probably using facets &amp; rites to screw people up)<br /> Pack Role: ?? (depends. are we doing the 'Alpha', 'Beta', 'Omega' thing? and also on who's who in-pack.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3070,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","user":"Barbrarilen","date":". 03-16-2015, 11:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T21:13:21-07:00","id":445306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Okami</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/442841-ooc-werewolf-2nd-ed-pbp-ooc-prep-with-dusksage-co?p=444627#post444627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So, after looking at those lovely pdf's in google doc I gotta ask how you did that, is the character sheet an interactive one from gone? and how does that whole googledoc thing work? Tis a mystery to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>CS came with the book. The background I wrote in Open Office and exported to pdf <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5337-soonmot","name":"soonmot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5337_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T23:26:21-07:00","id":445412,"title":"","content":"Here's mine. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'll sort background issues and my sheet when home from work.<br /> <br /> Name: Akule Harris<br /> Tribe: Hunter in Darkness<br /> Auspice: Full Moon<br /> RP Role: Defender<br /> Hunt Role: Harrying the prey, controlling the hunt<br /> Combat Role: Striking at weak points, heavy, fast assaults from concealment<br /> Pack Role: Oathkeeper<br /> <br /> Gift wise, I'm eying both all doors locked from Warding and Knotted paths from Nature. Those would let me control the prey in both a rural and urban setting depending on the hunting ground. The full moon gifts will supply the combat aspect of a Rahu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T00:04:21-07:00","id":445422,"title":"","content":"Name: Violet Caravell<br /> Tribe: Iron Masters<br /> Auspice: Irraka, New Moon<br /> RP Role: hesitant new comer<br /> Hunt Role: Forward scout/ spy<br /> Combat Role: Ambusher and bait<br /> Pack Role: Peacemaker","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5337-soonmot","name":"soonmot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5337_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T00:40:49-07:00","id":445431,"title":"","content":"Name: Indiana Annan<br /> Tribe: Hunters in Darkness<br /> Auspice: New Moon<br /> RP Role: Wild child, pack firebrand<br /> Hunt Role: Tracker, Harrier<br /> Combat Role: Assassination, sowing chaos, surgical strikes from darkness<br /> Pack Role: Problem solver, border patrol.<br /> <br /> Retias, I was also thinking of All Door Unlocked for Indiana, so let me know if you decide on it and I'll go another route. Maybe just Boundary Ward or Maze Ward instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T03:36:18-07:00","id":445556,"title":"","content":"What's everyone doing for rites? With only 2 dots, we don't have many options, I'm okay with &quot;donating&quot; my 2 dots to another character as long as someone is taking Chain Rage. Since we don't have a elodath, that rite is going to come in very handy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5337-soonmot","name":"soonmot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5337_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T03:50:53-07:00","id":445562,"title":"","content":"Name: Jospeh<br /> Tribe: Bone Shadows<br /> Auspice: Ithaeur<br /> RP Role: Devil's Advocate with a bit of Negotiator thrown in due to being in packs without Elodoth, plus the whole spirit advisement thing.<br /> Hunt Role: Cast Rites, Invoke Spirit allies, otherwise provide support using the Hisil and harrying prey<br /> Combat Role: Mostly Support and if given time to prepare Glass canon<br /> Pack Role: Pack Shaman<br /> <br /> Oh, for rites I've given him Message and Harness the Cycle, We'll need someone who can actually call the Siskur-Dah, Chain Rage is also a thing. :/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1705,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","user":"Okami","date":". 03-17-2015, 08:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T06:53:50-07:00","id":445745,"title":"","content":"I'm happy to be the Siskur Dah Ritemaster. I'll be investing a lot in rites anyway ^_^ It just means that before a hunt you're going to need to listen to one hell of a story. =)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T08:10:42-07:00","id":445897,"title":"","content":"As a Shaman I've got him split between a lot of rites and gifts. By the by, how strong are we looking at trying to make the totem? Cause I've got five whole merit dots there... Oh, and what kind of a totem do we want? Our characters will hunt it sure, but we can still design it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T09:17:46-07:00","id":446029,"title":"","content":"Violet will be pushing for a spirit that represents the city, nightlife, or major landmark. She's going to be a bit jealous of Joseph and his ability to speak with the spirits.<br /> <br /> Also: I edited in my explanations for my contacts and ally. Dusk, my ally is a vamp, but with one dot he's obviously not going to be hanging out with pack. He's mainly a source of gossip and someone to race through the city with. If this is still no good, I'll swap that dot out!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5337-soonmot","name":"soonmot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5337_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T09:55:29-07:00","id":446099,"title":"","content":"I see Joseph as looking for a spirit that reflects what he sees in the pack as a whole, but since they don't know each other that well he'll likely be defaulting to the common thread that ties them all i.e. their territory or something along the lines of a location. A major landmark he would find possible but it would depend on the other kinds of emotions that landmark represents. The spirit of the city itself he would find an intimidating but incredibly tempting option. He could definitely be sold on it. The jealousy thing though would likely go over his head. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T09:58:14-07:00","id":446100,"title":"","content":"A good way to do this by group consensus might be to each mention three aspects, or qualities, or characteristics you want the spirit/pack to have. Since we're an urban pack, Soonmot, I don't think you need to worry about it not representing the city in SOME fashion, so you so far suggested nightlife or a landmark in the area - throw in some other ideas if you like.<br /> <br /> Once we all put in our two cents, we'll organize them and see if anyone likes or can combine their characteristics and then we'll come up with an idea from there.<br /> <br /> For example:<br /> <br /> Since we don't have an Elodoth yet, I think I'd like an <i><b>influential </b></i>or <i><b>socially confident </b></i>totem who can help us pick up the slack with a strength we don't have too much of that ourselves.<br /> <br /> I also like the idea of a spirit <b><i>tied to a specific place</i></b> since it can help give us a dedicated locus, a base of operations, and really flavor what we as a group value and want to protect in Victory City.<br /> <br /> Thirdly, so far we have a very specialized bunch of people here - scouts and trackers and tacticians and defenders and 'support' with rites. We clearly aren't all about barreling in and being made of pure undestructablium, so I think our pack is putting an emphasis on <i><b>precise</b></i> <i><b>execution </b></i>as we tactically prepare with Aliza's visions to guide Violet's scouting and Indiana's skirmishing before Joseph backs up Akule with the big punch. Looking at what we have I'm a little worried we are too delicate... but then... we're werewolves. So probably not.<br /> <br /> (I'm going to make sure Aliza's got a high stamina at least - she might not hit hard either but she'll have more sufficient 'soak')","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T10:26:25-07:00","id":446129,"title":"","content":"I was planning on going with the Hunting Grounds rite, which is sort of a territory claiming rite and seems in line with my character. It's 2 dots so that's all I got. Also, I completely forgot about totem points. I can put 1-3 dots into that. I started with primal urge 2 so I don't have too much to work with.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 03-17-2015, 01:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T11:00:31-07:00","id":446186,"title":"","content":"I can pick up the chain rage rite and banish for my two. Rahu understand rage very well, after all. Amravanti, if you're planning on all doors unlocked, I'll shift my gift focus. I see Akule as acting as the pack's defender and meat shield, so I'm considering memento mori from the Death gift and pack stalks the prey from Stealth. Totem wise, something sociable seems wise. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> Connections wise, hm. For Joseph, Akule has also become separated from his family, though in his case it was by choice after killing his uncle with his first change hit. He may not have shared that with the pack yet though, it depends how long we've been together. Anyhow, he'd be a werewolf who's been without a pack for a fair while, and Joseph might have come across him that way.<br /> <br /> He works in a butcher, which might well be a place Violet has come across in her travels. Same with Indy perhaps, who he'd see as something of of a kindred spirit due to their tribe and shared focus on protection.<br /> <br /> I admit I'm not sure when it comes to Aliza. What do you all think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2650,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","user":"Retias","date":". 03-17-2015, 02:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T11:08:23-07:00","id":446203,"title":"","content":"I haven't even looked at gifts yet. There'll probably be at least one from Insight though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T11:21:22-07:00","id":446222,"title":"","content":"Excellent, excellent. So far this Pack is looking magnificent. <br /> <br /> Since the Pack has opted to hunt for their Totem I'm forbidding Totem as a merit at character creation so that way you'll need to invest exp that you earn from RP into this Totem.<br /> <br /> Also keep in mind these two key facts about your Pack: 1, this is going to be the lathes Pack of Uratha in the city. The Root Walkers were the largest with their numbers rumored to be at least six strong so since this is going to be a new Pack all eyes will be on your characters. 2, this pack was formed in response to the treaty of the Father since in the treaty it's stipulated that when one faction claims to form a new Pack the other side may do so as well. That means there will also be a new Pure Pack out there vying for a territory of their own as well as a Totem.<br /> <br /> In regards to the Seattle comment the Ithaeur of the Whisper Catchers warns the Forsaken about venturing there, saying simply that there's &quot;Too many angels.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T11:23:57-07:00","id":446229,"title":"","content":"Are there other rules to the treaty? Non-aggression, unity against the Beshilu and the like? I may delve into Mr Gone's sheets, if anyone ha a good link for one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T11:38:56-07:00","id":446331,"title":"","content":"Also, I'm going to start making my actual character sheet. Have a preferred format or place for those?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T11:52:16-07:00","id":446342,"title":"","content":"Treaty of the Father Rules<br /> <br /> 1. Make no treaspass into another's territory without first acquiring approval from that territory's alpha.<br /> <br /> 2. The enemies of Father Wolf are enemies to all the People. All information regarding the Hosts are to be shared freely among Father Wolf's children.<br /> <br /> 3. Each wolf's prey is their own and must take responsibility for their hunt should it endanger another Pack's territory.<br /> <br /> 4. Any oath breakers of the treaty are subject to the tribal laws of the accusser's Pack. Failure to adhere to the sentence of said tribal laws threaten the Treaty of the Wolf and their lives shall be forfeit.<br /> <br /> 5. Should a Pack fall and their territory become disputed between two or more Pack then a Sacred Challenge may be called so that one may rightfully claim said territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Edited 03-17-2015, 02:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T12:03:41-07:00","id":446350,"title":"","content":"Background: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1BfRH2Yjq7czS__QpbOmkE1yn00LJ73GsIQMz2eHPe6k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> Indiana works part time at a kennel. She is usually tasked with the more boisterous or aggressive animals as she has a way with them. Otherwise she's mostly patrolling the territory. She rents a room in a family's home and that's about it, though they never see her. She sleeps outside most nights anyway.She tends to be a bit obsessed with the remains of her father's burnt down church. If our locus were in or around there that would be convenient. I would make it her spiritual touchstone if the church itself were a locus. Otherwise I will work on that.<br /> <br /> Her physical touchstone is her father, who keeps trying to get in contact with her. Tries to get her to come home and clean up her life. He thinks she's joined a gang or is into some other type of trouble, which is sort of true in a sense, but obviously she can't tell him that.<br /> <br /> <br /> As far as pack connections. I can imagine an easy connection with Akule for the reasons Retias already mentioned. He is a defender and she is a bit reckless, but their goals and philosophy seem very similar so I can see them complementing each other nicely, especially on the hunt. Sort of a big brother-little sister (or vice versa) relationship.<br /> <br /> Violet and Indy are both young women and both Irraka I can see their relationship being either one of tension and disconnection because Indy can be very wild and Violet is very urban, or one of alliance, an odd couple friendship - a bond borne of being new moons, though they both embody it in slightly different ways. Let me know what you think, soonmot<br /> <br /> Eliza is an easy relationship for Indy. She's never had a mother, so she'll probably be very grateful for a parental figure. She'll probably not love her penchant for storytelling but there's a certain amount of leeway granted to the pack mom.<br /> <br /> Joseph I'm not sure yet. Probably mostly reverence, because despite being a werewolf for a while now, she was a lone wolf and ghost wolf for most of it so she probably doesn't have too much experience with the Shadow or spirits in general. His area of expertise is probably alien and a bit scary to her.<br /> <br /> <br /> As far as the Warding gifts, Retias. I would plan on <i>eventually</i> getting All Doors Unlocked, but I'm not starting with any Honor renown, so I wouldn't be able to start with it. So if you want to get it for our starting, that's perfectly fine with me. I am happy to just get the Boundary Ward or Maze Ward instead. Otherwise I'll pick it up pretty soon as it'd be an early priority for me, it's super useful during a hunt and one of us should have it for sure.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 03-17-2015, 03:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T12:10:04-07:00","id":446353,"title":"","content":"An abandoned church would be a cool HQ. That could be both a specific place and a socially-influential spirit, if the neighborhood still has fond memories of what used to be a real part of the community's heart, if we want to make our totem the spirit of the church? it constantly being threatened by spirits of ruin and neglect would be a pretty cool 'side-quest' for us, too ^_^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T12:27:18-07:00","id":446370,"title":"","content":"Ah, in that case Am, I'll drop my stealth gift pick for All doors Unlocked. I'm planning on a point of honor for my free renown pick, so it'd give me access to both it and memotir mori, which lets Akule absorb damage dealt to packmates and is very handy for the defender aspect.<br /> <br /> Really should make my sheet though..<br /> <br /> Touchstone wise, I'm thinking a cousin from his family who tries to keep in touch despite Akule's stubbornness there, someone he doesn't fully want to turn away despite his belief he's a risk to his family.<br /> <br /> Spiritual wise, hm.. I'll need to have a think.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T12:35:46-07:00","id":446397,"title":"","content":"Oh, is it Washington the state or the city?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T12:37:13-07:00","id":446398,"title":"","content":"Victory City, Washington State<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, facets are 2x Gibbous, as well as 'This Story is True' and 'Read the World's Loom'. =)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3070,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","user":"Barbrarilen","date":". 03-17-2015, 04:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T13:57:33-07:00","id":446511,"title":"","content":"Thanks! <br /> <br /> Appearance<br /> <br /> Aside from facial features that show his family's native origins, Akule doesn't tend to stand out in a crowd for the most part, preferring casual and reliable clothes that can manage a good amount of wear and tear. His hair is cropped short with a suggestion that he does it himself in front of a mirror, and has little caring for the rather uneven results.<br /> <br /> Personality<br /> <br /> Akule has been a rather defensive, often quite hostile young man since his First Change and the resulting death of a family member. While he's far from incapable of interacting with others, he's fairly wary of it and tends to keep it as limited as he can, with his current lack of trust in himself.<br /> <br /> What it has done is to harden his nature, though also provided the more positive merit of seeing him care about others he sees at risk, a desire to see some good be done closely tied to that.<br /> <br /> Background<br /> <br /> Akule isn't sure whether or not his name fully matches the history of the Colville tribe, but neither are his parents. However, in a small hint of cultural rebellion they settled on a name for him that didn't have such strong Anglican roots and made him stand out more. At times he enjoyed this, but at others, he found frustration at being put in a position that made him stand out. Still, that was far from his biggest issue.<br /> <br /> Spirits do not at all like the wolfblooded and Akule was tormented throughout his childhood by unseen forces that were a puzzle and concern both for him, and the community he grew up in. Ceremonies he took part in were disrupted in small, apparently petty ways and a number of his efforts to connect with others both inside and outside of his local, small community also tended to end badly, to the point where certain, mean spirited others began calling him 'Runs-with-Coyote' behind his back. This did not at all improve his moods as he grew older.<br /> <br /> Born and raised in Victory City, he wound up in a number of incidents as he grew older, culminating in a series of rough fights that got him a sharp warning from both his own elders and the police that interrupted the street based tussle. Sixteen, that time he managed to avoid juvenile court, with a warning he would be unlikely to have that luck next time. In an effort to work out some of his tension, his uncle started to take him on camping trips during the holiday periods with other youth who had an interest in exploring historical practices. They hunted, explored and listened to stories in a refreshing break from the mundane nature of day to day life.<br /> <br /> Until four years later, where Akule's uncle died.<br /> <br /> Akule only has scattered memories of the time, but it's enough for him to know what truly happened there. He and Jonas had been tracking a deer, the man having decided to use it as an excuse to try and get to the bottom of his nephew's recent, excessive mood swings. However, the second an arrow pierced the deer's side and spilled blood on the earth, Akule saw red.<br /> <br /> He remembers his uncle screaming for mercy, the blood on his claws and the red, ugly rage. Finer details escape him, but when it was over, Jonas was very much dead and Akule was huddled on the ground in a naked, bloody, weeping heap. The others concluded the two of them had been attacked by a dangerous predator, and Akule's garbled account of events was put down to the harrowing of his experience and witnessing his uncle's death. Aware of the far worse truth, Akule almost immediately left his family and friends behind and retreated into his own place in the city, cutting off contact with his previous life and taking up a low paying job as a butcher.<br /> <br /> It was in that self imposed exile that others of the Forsaken would find him.<br /> <br /> Sheet:<br /> <br /> <b>Name:</b> Akule Harris<br /> <b>Age:</b> 20<br /> <b>Blood:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Warden</b> -<br /> <br /> You protect. Territory, packmates, loci. Whatever a Warden swore to protect, you'll sooner walk over their cold, dead body before you harm it.<br /> <br /> Your character regains a point of Willpower whenever he puts the object of his protection above his well-being or comfort. He regains all spent Willpower whenever he preemptively hunts would be aggressors, or uses <i>Kuruth</i> to ward off the danger to those he protects.<br /> <br /> <b>Bone:</b><br /> <br /> Cub\u2014 The Cub hasn\u2019t quite finished baking. She isn\u2019t ready to take on full responsibility for herself, and relies on<br /> the help of others to get by. Her own answers aren\u2019t the best, so she leans on others\u2019 answers to get by.<br /> <br /> Your character recovers a point of Willpower when she ignores her own impulses in favor of another\u2019s advice. She regains all Willpower when she puts life and limb completely into another\u2019s hands, when she could alternatively use the blood of the wolf to achieve her goals<br /> <br /> <b>Auspice:</b> Rahu<br /> <b>Tribe:</b> Hunters in Darkness<br /> <b>Aspirations:<br /> Settle things with his cousin<br /> Hunt down remnants of the Beshilu<br /> Find satisfaction with both his human life and the hunt<br /> Triggers:</b><br /> <br /> PACK<br /> Passive: A pack member takes lethal damage.<br /> Common: Seeing someone attack a pack member.<br /> Specific: You cause lethal damage to a pack member.<br /> <br /> <b>Touchstones:</b><br /> The Cousin (Physical). Marcus insists on visiting Akule despite the other's self imposed exile, partly because of how close the cousin's were, but partly as the werewolf's extreme silence makes him think there's more to the death of his father then he knows.<br /> <br /> The Prey (Spiritual). Akule well knows the damage the Beshilu can do if left unchecked, and most of his hunting focus has turned on them.<br /> <br /> <b>Attributes</b><br /> Strength 3 (4/6/5/3) \u2022 Dexterity 2 (2/3/4/4) \u2022 Stamina 3 (4/5/5/4)<br /> Intelligence 2 \u2022 Wits 2 \u2022 Resolve 3<br /> Presence 2 \u2022 Manipulation 2 (1/2/1/1) \u2022 Composure 2<br /> <br /> <b>Skills</b> (Mental; -3 unskilled) Academics 0 \u2022 Computer 0 \u2022 Crafts 3 (Food) \u2022 Investigation 2 \u2022 Medicine 2 \u2022 Occult 0 \u2022 Politics 0 \u2022 Science 0 (Physical; -1 unskilled) Athletics 3 (Archery) \u2022 Brawl 4 (Tooth and claw) \u2022 Drive 0 \u2022 Firearms 0 \u2022 Larceny 0 \u2022 Stealth 3 \u2022 Survival 2 \u2022 Weaponry 0 (Social; -1 unskilled) Animal Ken 2 \u2022 Empathy 0 \u2022 Expression 0 \u2022 Intimidation 2 \u2022 Persuasion 0 \u2022 Socialize 0 \u2022 Streetwise 0 \u2022 Subterfuge 0<br /> <br /> <b>Merits</b><br /> Language (First Tongue) 1<br /> <br /> Resources 1<br /> Creative tactician 3<br /> Nowhere to hide 2<br /> Efficient killer 2<br /> Relentless assault FS 2<br /> <br /> Gifts:<br /> <br /> Full moon 2<br /> Warding (Honor)<br /> Death (Honor)<br /> <br /> <b>Rites</b> <br /> <br /> Chain rage 1<br /> Banish 1<br /> <br /> <b>Renown</b><br /> Cunning<br /> Glory<br /> Honor 1<br /> Purity 2<br /> Wisdom<br /> <br /> <b>Advantages</b><br /> Size: 5 (6/7/6/4)<br /> Speed: 10 (11/14/17/15)<br /> Defense: 5 (5/5/5/5)<br /> Initiative: 4 (4/5/6/6)<br /> Health: 8 (10/12/11/8)<br /> Willpower: 5<br /> Harmony: 7<br /> Primal Urge: 1<br /> Essence: 10/1<br /> <br /> <b>Equipment</b><br /> <br /> <b>Experiences</b><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T14:19:49-07:00","id":446532,"title":"","content":"<i>There's a saying among librarians, 'three moves is a fire' - that is to say, if you have to keep moving and shifting and unpacking the stuff you try to keep in order, you are going to wind up with a whole lot of it being destroyed by good intentions.<br /> <br /> Aliza was pretty sure that saying should apply to people as well. She was in her second year of school trying to get her Master's to be a librarian, in her third apartment since she had started, looking for a fourth nearby temp job to help the bills since setting out. Bad luck just kept on following her now. The things she saw in dark corners were bad enough, but these days it was like the weird shapes and ghosts were </i>noticing <i>her. And when things started noticing, things started breaking. Water mains, contracts, favorite professors' backs when they slipped on ice. And then classes were canceled and Aliza started to work on transferring credits again.<br /> <br /> When the hallucinations progressed to nightmares - of black pools and hot flesh and frantic chasing and the taste of blood in her mouth - Aliza figured that the fire had happened, and one extra move or change was just one too many. That third apartment never had a chance as her first howl shattered glass and stone and plaster while she savaged the dozens of spirits of misfortune that had settled around her, scattering them to the winds. At least now she can name her problems. Describe them and laugh at them and make them an easy pill to swallow so others learn from her mistake. She wanted to be a librarian to help guide other people to what they needed to know. Now she listens to the Moon and the whispers in the shadows, and does the same. </i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Name</b>: Aliza Carter<br /> <br /> <b>Concept</b>: Visionary Matron<br /> <br /> <b>Tribe</b>: Bone Shadow<br /> <b>Auspice</b>: Cahalith<br /> <br /> <br /> Aliza Carter is all about being a font of knowledge and direction for her pack. She may not be the Alpha, but she'll still be the mother, telling her tales and delving into darkness to find the truths she can return to them to help grant direction and strength. She has deep and abiding respect for the unity of pack and the various roles and burdens her brethren must carry, but her strength is also her weakness -- if her pack is fractured and cannot share its responsibilities, she will reach too far, and too quickly, taking the weight upon herself, collapsing and dragging the others along with her as she falls apart under the strain.<br /> <br /> She is a compact woman of mixed European decent - her Portuguese blood runs strongest, in wavy dark hair and a slightly less than imposing stature - all the better to draw others in close to listen to her tales.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Aspirations:</b><br /> <br /> Short-Term <i>Earn a pack to call her own</i>.<br /> Mid-Term <i>Build herself up so she is stronger and more secure</i>.<br /> Long-Term <i>Teach the world a glorious new lesson all her own</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Attributes</b>:<br /> <br /> <i>Physical</i><br /> Strength \u2022\u2022<br /> Dexterity \u2022\u2022<br /> Stamina \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <br /> <i>Mental</i><br /> Intelligence \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> Wits \u2022\u2022<br /> Resolve \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <br /> <i>Social</i><br /> Presence \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> Manipulation \u2022<br /> Composure \u2022\u2022<br /> <br /> <b>Skills </b><br /> <br /> <i>Physical</i><br /> Athletics \u2022\u2022<br /> Brawl \u2022<br /> Stealth \u2022<br /> Survival \u2022<br /> <br /> <i>Mental</i><br /> Academics \u2022\u2022 (Libraries/Research)<br /> Investigation \u2022\u2022<br /> Occult \u2022\u2022<br /> Politics \u2022<br /> <br /> <i>Social</i><br /> Empathy \u2022\u2022<br /> Expression \u2022\u2022\u2022* (Storytelling) (* = Auspice dot)<br /> Persuasion \u2022\u2022<br /> Socialize \u2022\u2022<br /> Streetwise \u2022\u2022<br /> <br /> Cahalith Bone Shadow<br /> <i>Hirfathra Hissu - 'Pay Each Spirit In Kind'</i><br /> <br /> <u>Blood</u>: <i>Beta</i><br /> The Beta wolf desire order. When the pack works, like a well oiled machine, nothing can stand in it's way. And to do that, every single member of the pack must be operating at their best. The Beta feels their position in the pack is to make this happen. For them, the Pack comes first, before anything. Even themselves. Your character recovers a point of Willpower when she makes sure a packmate can perform at the top of her game, while disregarding her personal interests. Your character replenishes all spent Willpower when she puts herself in mortal danger or fall to Kuruth for the sake of her pack.<br /> <br /> <u>Bone</u>: <i>Maker</i><br /> You want to leave a mark in the world. You wish to create something of lasting value. Bring together a Protectorate, a Lodge, tend to a growing locus, or maybe, form the next Tribe. Your character regains a point of Willpower whenever he tends to his project to the exclusion of his pack given duties. He regains all spent willpower when he disregards a Hunt in favor of his project.<br /> <br /> <u>Touchstones</u>:<br /> <i>Physical</i>- Aliza still wants a library. Even if she doesn't need to be a librarian anymore - being a lorekeeper and seer is pretty much awesome enough - she still has a strong urge to have a safe space for herself that she can fill with valuable things and keep and share with others.<br /> <i>Spiritual</i>- (The Lune) - When the Moon showed Aliza the truth her eyes had been missing for so long, it sparked something deep within her. A need, to not only gather truth, but to create it - to be an example, to use her gifts, to tell a tale, to create a legend --- the world is not a pleasant one, nor an easy one. Its a world on the cusp of a thousand little wars, any one of which may be ripening towards her legend - in her ear it was whispered that the Cahalunim of Victory City would be watching, eager to see her story.<br /> <br /> <u>Triggers</u><br /> <br /> <i>Passive</i>: A werewolf you don\u2019t know enters your territory without permission.<br /> <i>Common</i>:Seeing someone attack a pack member<br /> <i>Specific</i>: You cause lethal damage to a pack member<br /> <br /> <b>Gifts</b>:<br /> <br /> <i>Moon Gifts</i><br /> <br /> <u>War Howl</u> (\u2022)<br /> <br /> <i>The Cahalith howls her defiance and spurs her pack to greater heights of violence and fury.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Cost</i>: 1 Essence <i>Dice Pool</i>: Presence + Expression + Glory<br /> <i>Action</i>: Instant <i>Duration</i>: 1 turn per success<br /> <br /> <i>Dramatic Failure</i>: A single enemy who can hear the howl regains 1 spent Willpower point.<br /> <i>Failure</i>: The Cahalith\u2019s howl fails to inspire her pack.<br /> <i>Success</i>: All members of the Cahalith\u2019s pack within earshot gain +1L rating on their Brawl and Weaponry attacks for the duration of the Facet. This bonus damage is always lethal, even if the attack deals bashing damage.<br /> <i>Exceptional Success</i>: The Cahalith gains the <b>Inspired </b>Condition.<br /> <br /> <u>Voice of Glory</u> (\u2022\u2022)<br /> <br /> <i>The voice of the Cahalith is powerful, reassuring, and inspiring. She holds audiences in thrall to her words, both her allies and hapless prey who don\u2019t understand the threat she poses.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Cost</i>: 1 Essence <i>Action</i>: Instant <i>Duration</i>: 1 scene<br /> <br /> The Cahalith adds her Glory Renown to her all dice pools for Expression and Persuasion. If using this Gift when meeting someone for the first time, the Cahalith automatically improves her first impression (p. 164) by one step. If she is attempting to inspire or incite violence and aggression, increase her impression by another step.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Shadow Gifts</i><br /> <br /> <u>This Story is True</u> (Glory)<br /> <br /> <i>Tales of the past can teach important lessons in the present. It doesn\u2019t matter if the story is factually true, as long as the symbolic meaning is true enough.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Cost</i>: 2 Essence <i>Dice Pool</i>: Presence + Academics + Glory<br /> <i>Action</i>: Instant <i>Duration</i>: 1 hour per success<br /> <br /> When the Uratha uses this Facet, she relates a story that has an important meaning or lesson pertaining to a current problem or challenge. She may grant the story\u2019s lesson to herself or to one packmate who hears her words. The story doesn\u2019t need to be long, but it does need to deliver its point clearly.<br /> <br /> <i>Dramatic Failure</i>: The Uratha suffers the Ban Condition. She feels compelled to speak entirely in stories and verse, answering even the simplest of questions with poetry, meandering tales, or rhyme.<br /> <i>Failure</i>: The Facet fails.<br /> <i>Success</i>: The Facet grants a number of dots equal to successes rolled in a single skill that the target has two or fewer dots in. This Story Is True cannot raise a skill above five dots.<br /> <br /> The Uratha may not use this Facet on more than one target at a time; attempting to do so immediately removes the previously bestowed skill dots.<br /> <br /> <u>Read the World's Loom</u> (Glory)<br /> <br /> <i>The world is filled with a deluge of seemingly trivial information that offers insight to the initiated.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Cost</i>: 5 Essence <i>Dice Pool</i>: Wits + Streetwise + Glory <i>Action</i>: Instant<br /> <br /> If this Facet is used while the Uratha is in his pack\u2019s territory, its cost is reduced to 3 Essence.<br /> <br /> Roll Results<br /> <br /> <i>Dramatic Failure</i>: The Uratha reads a false message in his surroundings; a flight of birds makes him fear a hostile pack approaches when no such threat exists.<br /> <i>Failure</i>: The Facet fails.<br /> <i>Success</i>: The Uratha gains insight from his surroundings, hearing of a coming threat from the growling engines of a traffic jam, reading secrets from amidst the gang tags on the walls, or seeing the sorry state of the Gauntlet in the patterns of scurrying cockroaches. The character learns of a single event, threat, or circumstance of meaningful relevance to the Uratha<br /> within his Glory Renown in miles. The information gained relates to the present or the near future, although anything beyond 24 hours is likely to be extremely vague.<br /> <br /> Topics that the character can choose to have insight into (along with sample answers) include:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Threats. (The police chief is planning a raid on the pack; werewolves come seeking a showdown; the tenement is unstable and will soon collapse; the old spirit Thurizag has returned)<br /> \u2022 The supernatural. (Something preys on human residents in the area; something dwells in the high-rise; something numbs the minds of residents)<br /> \u2022 The Gauntlet. (It lies in tatters; swathes are thick and stifling; spirits are breaching it)<br /> \u2022 The Shadow. (Someone is cultivating a particular spiritual resonance; the umia are at war; interlopers have entered the Shadow)<br /> \u2022 Violence. (A riot is brewing; there is a pattern to the murders; a hunt is taking place)<br /> \u2022 Conflicts. (Gangs are feuding over drug territory; the big corporation is under financial attack, the mayoral election is turning nasty)<br /> \u2022 Weather. (A storm is coming; the blazing heat will not abate for a week; the heavy rain hides murders)<br /> <br /> If the character chooses a topic to which there are no meaningful answers, he can choose a different topic instead.<br /> <br /> <i>Exceptional Success</i>: The Uratha can choose two topics to gain insight into.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Rites</b>:<br /> <br /> <i>Sacred Hunt </i>(\u2022\u2022)<br /> <br /> The Sacred Hunt, the <i>Siskur-Dah</i>, is the most holy of all rites. Many werewolves believe that it draws upon the laws of the hunt that the Wolf-Mother herself personified.<br /> <i>Symbols</i>: The hunt, prey, claws or weapons, blood<br /> <i>Action</i>: Extended (10 successes; each roll represents 1 minute)<br /> <br /> Mechanically, Aliza rolls Presence + Expression: Narrative-wise, she tells the tale she and her pack are about to act out -- the righteousness of their cause, the truth of the situation, and the depth of their need. She lets her words light a fire in their hearts, and sends them forth with a whisper sent straight to their souls.<br /> <br /> <i>Success</i>: The rite binds hunters and prey into the Siskur-Dah. All werewolves present are cast as the hunters. The ritemaster must indicate the intended prey during the rite, which can be an individual or a group, but they do not need to be identified with precise details or names.<br /> <br /> The rite has three effects:<br /> <br /> All participating werewolves gain the Siskur-Dah Condition.<br /> <br /> If the Uratha bring down a spirit that is the prey of this rite, they may divide its remaining Essence amongst themselves as they see fit; this can be used to destroy a spirit by draining all its Essence and discorporating it, but doing so is usually a breaking point toward Spirit and is seen as disrespectful if done without good reason.<br /> <br /> If the Uratha chase down spirit-prey that knows the symbols of a rite or can carve the secret of a Gift, any Uratha hunter present can expend the necessary Experiences to be marked with the Gift or learn the rite from the spirit. If this is done, the hunters do not get any Essence if they then bring the spirit down, and doing so is a breaking point toward Spirit.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Renown</b>:<br /> <i>Wisdom </i>\u2022<br /> <i>Glory </i>\u2022\u2022<br /> <br /> <b>Merits</b>: \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><i>Seven dots remaining - waiting to see what else we need before I invest in Aliza herself. Can we trade merit dots for other things? Do we get that dot of Totem to put elsewhere?</i></span><br /> <br /> <i>Song in Your Heart </i>(\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <br /> Prerequisites: Glory \u2022\u2022<br /> <br /> Effect: Your character sings, howls, and tells stories like none other. Her words echo and reverberate through listeners, and inspire them to learn from her tales. This Merit acts as the Inspiring Merit (see p. 111). Your character does not need to meet the prerequisites for that Merit, and it can only be used when singing, howling, or storytelling. Listeners may take the Inspired Condition (see p. 308) as a Persistent Condition, gaining a Beat every time they take a significant action inspired by your character\u2019s tale.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Willpower = 5<br /> Harmony = 7<br /> Size = 6<br /> Health = 8<br /> Defense = 4<br /> Primal Urge = 1","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3070,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","user":"Barbrarilen","date":". 03-17-2015, 05:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T16:12:11-07:00","id":446663,"title":"","content":"I like your idea Bar, Joseph will agree with an <b>influential</b> spirit, but he'll stretch that farther by saying since they are a larger than normal pack with a lot of potential they'll need a totem to match, which means he'll want to go for a lesser Jaggling. Its true that's a huge risk for a Forsaken pack, but that's why he'll want the pack to take it. Privately whether or not they can even pull it off would be his personal litmus test for if they can even work as a pack. The point with him is that a normal totem wont be able to adequately support the pack due to its unusual size, they'll need something already respected among a decent amount of spirits to keep a lot of the smaller spiritual problems in line with their new territory. Stat-wise I think this works too, if we <i>were</i> investing points it would only take everyone at two and one at three to pull the rank off, and I like the idea of needing to RP it out.<br /> <br /> Should get a character sheet up soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T16:42:07-07:00","id":446692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Okami</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/442841-ooc-werewolf-2nd-ed-pbp-ooc-prep-with-dusksage-co?p=446663#post446663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like your idea Bar, Joseph will agree with an <b>influential</b> spirit, but he'll stretch that farther by saying since they are a larger than normal pack with a lot of potential they'll need a totem to match, which means he'll want to go for a lesser Jaggling. Its true that's a huge risk for a Forsaken pack, but that's why he'll want the pack to take it. Privately whether or not they can even pull it off would be his personal litmus test for if they can even work as a pack. The point with him is that a normal totem wont be able to adequately support the pack due to its unusual size, they'll need something already respected among a decent amount of spirits to keep a lot of the smaller spiritual problems in line with their new territory. Stat-wise I think this works too, if we <i>were</i> investing points it would only take everyone at two and one at three to pull the rank off, and I like the idea of needing to RP it out.<br /> <br /> Should get a character sheet up soon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh dude we will die. I think building a spirit up until it can take a jaggling on would be better than trying to beat one into submission right out the gate.<br /> <br /> Think of it more like a Pokemon battle :-P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T17:52:51-07:00","id":446813,"title":"","content":"Just realized I hadn't posted my character sheet. <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BxK0La5plUm8VUZXcjBKRjlqT28/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Here it is</a>. I want to get rid of Fleet of Foot, because I know Violet's whole thing is city running, but I honestly don't know what else to get. Any rites we still need? Sounded like we had it covered.<br /> And here is my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1BfRH2Yjq7czS__QpbOmkE1yn00LJ73GsIQMz2eHPe6k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">background</a> again.<br /> <br /> I'll explain the stuff that needs more explaining here.<br /> <br /> <b>Blood:</b> The Monster \u2014 A Monster revels in the shadows, using terror and shock to cripple the victims of his hunts. It\u2019s less important to overwhelm a victim by force than it is to overwhelm it psychologically. By the time his jaws clamp down, the fight should already be over. Your character recovers a point of Willpower when he resorts to disgusting or frightening someone into submission. He recovers all Willpower when using the hunt or Kuruth as a terror tactic.<br /> <b>Bone:</b> The Martyr \u2014 The Martyr is always willing to take the risk herself. She knows that sometimes what needs to be done is too dangerous for her pack. She\u2019s not a lone wolf, but she\u2019s much more willing to take a risk herself if she feels it\u2019s the best recourse. Your character recovers a point of Willpower when she acts independently of her pack to solve a pack problem. She regains all Willpower when her pack is on the hunt, chooses not to take a specific risk, and she subverts their plans and takes the risk on her own.<br /> <br /> <i>[I made her Bone an altered version of The Lone Wolf Bone, because it didn't quite represent her the way I wanted. Let me know if anyone can think of any tweaks to make it work better, or if it's fine as is. It's just supposed to represent her willingness to sacrifice herself for the greater good or assume risk so that her pack doesn't have to.]</i><br /> <br /> Touchstones.<br /> Physical: The Parents - Her father just wants her to come home. Leave whatever gang she's joined up with, clean herself up. He stops by her work every now and then, though usually she sees him coming and slips out. It's not that she doesn't want to see him, it's just that he wouldn't understand. He still thinks she's his little girl. He'd still expect her to keep a curfew, to worship on Sundays.<br /> <br /> Spiritual: The Locus - The burned down church that she spent so much time in over the years is comforting. It's not just the memories, or clinging to the life she lost after the change, it's something different. This place is sacred. Not just in the way everyone else thinks. The place is a locus. Not just that, but it favours her. She spends hours in the Shadow, bathing in the purity of its essence. Some might say she's addicted. She'll only say that it's a place that needs to be protected. And no one is going to take it from her.<br /> <br /> [Of course I can change this spiritual touchstone if we end up not going with the church]<br /> <br /> <br /> Rites:<br /> <b>Hunting Ground </b>(2 dots)<br /> <br /> This rite invokes the old rights of Father Wolf to sanctify a claim of territory and ownership. The Shadow must bow before Urfarah even now.<br /> <br /> <b>Action</b>: Extended (10 successes; each roll represents half an hour)<br /> <b>Duration</b>: 1 season<br /> <b>Success</b>: The area is sanctified as the pack\u2019s territory. Certain Facets and Rites are affected by territory. All pack members gain a +2 bonus to foot chases and tracking while in their territory, whether in pursuit or escape. All pack members also gain a +2 bonus to Animal Ken, Empathy, and Politics<br /> rolls made on inhabitants. If the pack fails to complete at least one hunt each month, whether normal or Siskur-Dah, the rite immediately ends.<br /> <br /> <i>[I'm not actually sure if this rite is <b>necessary</b> to claim a territory or just makes it official, but I'm not taking any risks.]</i><br /> <br /> Aspirations:<br /> <b>Disband or root out local gang</b> - While the gang that burned down her father's house has long since disbanded, another has simply taken its place. Indiana plans to bring them down some day, or at least get them out of her territory.<br /> <b>Find a new family</b> - Indiana has felt adrift in her own home since she changed. She longs to feel part of a family again. She longs for this pack to feel like home.<br /> <b>Give in to Kuruth</b> - Indiana has never given in to Death Rage. A part of her longs to give in to the pure release of rage. The wiser side of her knows that this is reckless and dangerous. She knows she would never willingly put herself in that situation, of course. She's smarter than that. But still, all the frustration and anger she feels roiling inside her needs an outlet. Nothing has ever been enough to vent the anger she feels in her heart for the people who have done her family harm. The people who continue to defile her territory. She has found herself skirting the edge of death rage, but always managed to pull herself back. But what if she didn't.. would that be so bad? She tells herself she would regret it, but sometimes, she is not sure.<br /> <br /> <i>[The last aspiration is also something I'm not sure about. I like the idea behind it, but does it count as an aspiration if she's actively avoiding it? Not sure. Second one might be too vague. Let me know what you guys think if you can.]</i><br /> <br /> Triggers:<br /> Passive - Being in the area of a wound.<br /> Common - Seeing someone attack a pack member (risky, I know)<br /> Specific - A werewolf you don't know challenges your pack's ability to do it's duty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 03-17-2015, 10:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T17:59:08-07:00","id":446816,"title":"","content":"I'm okay with whatever level of spirit you guys want to go after. A jaggling would be pretty rough, but I'm not afraid to risk it if you guys want to. One thing though, I'm not sure our pack is of an unusual size. We have 5 player characters (unless any of the people from the other thread show up or something) and no NPC'S so far as far as I can tell. I'm not sure if I have any NPC's to suggest adding to the pack, but I'll think about it. Either way, that leaves us at 5 right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":".  Don't know why I thought Violet's ally was a Wolf Blooded. 03-17-2015, 09:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T18:58:44-07:00","id":446882,"title":"","content":"Wow, ok for some reason I was convinced we had 7 people... My brain I don't even, well, nonetheless, you what they say go big or go home. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Seriously though, how is everyone separating the character sheet from the pdf? I can't figure that out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T19:07:05-07:00","id":446887,"title":"","content":"I guess they're printing it out as a pdf and editing it. I should do that &gt;_&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T19:09:48-07:00","id":446890,"title":"","content":"You guys can just go to <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/145541/Werewolf-the-Forsaken-2nd-Edition\" target=\"_blank\">drivethrurpg </a>or a couple other places and below the link for the 2nd Edition book you can download the editable version of the character sheet. Then all you have to do is edit it and upload it somewhere and you're done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T20:21:54-07:00","id":446984,"title":"","content":"Well, in case I miss counted out players then I'm locking the game now. Those who've posted ideas or full blown characters are locked in as players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T21:42:45-07:00","id":447119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/442841-ooc-werewolf-2nd-ed-pbp-ooc-prep-with-dusksage-co?p=446692#post446692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh dude we will die. I think building a spirit up until it can take a jaggling on would be better than trying to beat one into submission right out the gate.<br /> <br /> Think of it more like a Pokemon battle :-P</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmm... To be honest I have no idea how fighting it mechanically would work, but I thought it'd be neat to go for and I expected the ST to go &quot;lol no&quot; if we were contemplating suicide. If you guys think its impossible of course I'm up for something else. This is my first dive into an actual WoD game instead of just reading so I defer to more experienced players OOC. Won't lie though, super tempted to go for it. We don't necessarily have to just fight it out from the get-go. For instance we could spend most of the hunt itself just trying to find the ban and bane, prepping a site to our advantage wheeling and dealing with other spirits for support, harry it while avoiding an actual fight till we could take it on. Tough, risky, but to actually pull it off... Still though as I said, if this thing really is on another level to the point that this is crazy I'm definitely fine with changing my mind. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T21:49:40-07:00","id":447126,"title":"","content":"Naw, its more... the reason I said it was like a pokemon battle. It isn't so much fighting it as convincing it to accept us! If its a big-enough nasty-enough spirit, and we bind ourselves to it, a pack of baby werewolves isn't going to really be able to keep up with its demands, I think! Then what do we do when it gets angry?! : O","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T23:21:07-07:00","id":447207,"title":"","content":"A lot of siprits can't be fought directly, I think you need to use bans, strategy, understanding their nature etc. The key is to show our would be totem that joining with us matches its nature and purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T01:50:18-07:00","id":447385,"title":"","content":"I really like the church spirit idea. A defeated, harried spirit that needs the pack as much as we need it. Something we can help grow more powerful while using its influence to affect our territory in a positive manner.<br /> <br /> Barb: I'll &quot;trade&quot; you my two dots of rites for 2 of your merit dots if Dusk is okay with that. I am lacking in contacts.<br /> <br /> Amra: Don't worry about stepping on toes, if fleet of foot works for your character, take it. If Indy is faster than Vi, that will just push Violet to improve! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> So, character links, Violet goes all over the city, so she could convievably meet everyone anywhere.<br /> Indy: I like the idea of being cautious friends. Indy loves the rage, Violet is afraid of it. Violet is about remaining unseen and avoiding conflict while Indy revels in it. They compliment each other well. Vi also has links to gang culture in the city and can help with that aspiration.<br /> <br /> <br /> Aliza: Violet's mom died (of natural causes) before Vi's change, so a mother figure, especially one that genuinely cares is a person who she'd value greatly. Violet could have Aliza at the library.<br /> <br /> Joseph: Might find Vi annoying. She doesn't really understand spirits but is *really* interested in them. Probably pesters him constantly about making her bicycle into a spirit since she thinks that'll turn it into some sort of magical pet.<br /> <br /> <br /> Akule: Violet likes this guy because he might know even less about being a werewolf than she does, but isn't afraid to ask questions, plus, when fights starts, she knows who to hide behind while setting up another strike.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm off work the next two nights, so I'll be making Grace from Violet's first change story into a wolf blooded as well some humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5337-soonmot","name":"soonmot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5337_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T06:41:55-07:00","id":447636,"title":"","content":"Amravanti, what denomination of faith is your character's father's church? I'd like to write up a proposed spirit, any details you can provide would help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T07:16:34-07:00","id":447651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/442841-ooc-werewolf-2nd-ed-pbp-ooc-prep-with-dusksage-co?p=447126#post447126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Naw, its more... the reason I said it was like a pokemon battle. It isn't so much fighting it as convincing it to accept us! If its a big-enough nasty-enough spirit, and we bind ourselves to it, a pack of baby werewolves isn't going to really be able to keep up with its demands, I think! Then what do we do when it gets angry?! : O</div> </div> </div> </div>You just need to win some battles with it and give it lots of pokeblocks! =D<br /> <br /> A lesser Jaggling though, from what I know, while difficult wouldn't be too hard to keep as a totem, its just hard to earn that first bit of begrudging respect. If this were a greater Jaggling like a lot of Pure go for I'd agree with you, those things are scary. Like the difference between a plotting minor noble in a religious city state and the head priest who privately thinks he's divine. The first you can negotiate and maybe you might even come to trust each other and the dude could grow to even see you as an equal. The latter? D=<br /> <br /> Honestly though it just sounds like a challenge, which just makes me want to do it more. Character-wise I see Joseph as an Ithaeur who is worried about they're status as a new pack. He doesn't trust the treaty with the Pure to not dissolve back to violence soon, and this is on top of the Beshilu infestation means they're a pack fighting for territory, looking like a target. He doesn't feel they have time to slowly establish themselves. Taking on a spirit like this is showing what they can do and whether or not they can manage in such a volatile place. If they pull it off they also gain an amazing packmate.<br /> <br /> Pro tip; he might be totally privately enamoured as a young Ithaeur with the notion of a spirit packmate, regardless of rank, he just believes as werewolves they can be good enough to pull it off. (which might be arrogance on his part)<br /> <br /> In terms of impressions of packmates based off what I've read so far?<br /> <br /> Violet; &quot;You want me to <i>what</i> with your bike so it will <i>what?</i> Werewolf, what you doing? Werewolf, <i>staaaaaaaaaaaaaaahp</i>.&quot; k, so that might have been a little OOC.<br /> <br /> Aliza; As a fellow Bone Shadow and a Cahalith Joseph will see her as a combination of an invaluable resource on the Spirits (storyteller or not she should be interested in the truth yes?) and the only other person who gets how important spirits can be even if she's not as aware of them as he is.<br /> <br /> Akule; Joseph will just hope he's willing to listen, but he also knows Rahu can be invaluable packmates of incredible discipline.<br /> <br /> Idianna; Irraka are dependable, and Indianna seems that way, he just hopes she doesnt forget their are other was of seeing besides eyes, and there's always something watching. He may also take to calling her Jones or Jonesy, this is not my fault. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1705,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","user":"Okami","date":". 03-18-2015, 10:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T07:46:07-07:00","id":447671,"title":"","content":"Indy's father would have been Protestant, he would have been a bit nontraditional as far as Pastors go, probably not too strict on the rules of religion, with more focus on the people and community - but the church itself would have been far older than him. It would have been a really old church, possibly one of, if not <i>the</i> oldest in the city, that had fallen into disrepair (possibly not for the first time in its history). Indiana's father purchased and renovated it with his life's savings and brought it back to some of its former glory through emphasizing the sense of community that it provided the neighbourhood. He made it a place where everyone could gather and see their neighbours in a time when connecting with the community is rarer and rarer. The inside is char and ash, but the building could be still standing structurally. Maybe with a collapsed vestry or chapel. Maybe it looks fine from the front, but the back is entirely burned out.<br /> <br /> <br /> These are just some ideas. Feel free to change any of that as it suits you, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T08:18:17-07:00","id":447724,"title":"","content":"Hm, okay. A couple of thoughts:<br /> <br /> 1) obviously I love the idea of the church, it'll be a cool spirit in general, so all of this is more of a 'please convince me otherwise'<br /> <br /> --- Indy might be too connected to the church for it to be our base of operations if your father is still in the area? unless we make him wolf-blooded too! ^_- Or if after the fire, maybe her family moved out to the suburb, but she stayed? could help keep you independent for story purposes. You might want to at least uncouple some of the ties to it -- if he bought it with his life savings, there's no way we're going to have access to it unless he's comfortable with us. It might just be that's where he preached and the protestant community stopped supporting it once it burned down, so he was moved elsewhere? Doesn't change the family connection to the place, just how it is here in the present, now that we're around.<br /> <br /> --- Dusk, thoughts on how we could claim the church outside of squatting in it? I don't think we'd want to live in a burnt out husk forever, so if we started making repairs to make it liveable, we'd also be noticeable... and need to be able to keep people out, sort of.<br /> <br /> --- Then again if the church is not only our totem but also a dedicated locus (confession, I LOVE the idea of having this really special 'heart' of our territory that we need to protect) then it having public access might be a good thing for us - people in positive moods that come to like, a garden we put where the collapsed section was, it feeds the locus keeps the essence flowing?<br /> <br /> --- how much do you think that will conflict with the separation between the People and the Herd?<br /> <br /> --- oaths and bans with a church are going to be tricky. depending on the actual spirit - it could be a faith spirit, a building/architeture spirit, a community spirit... generally speaking I think we're thinking of 'whatever the ruling spirit over the place is' -- and that means it has to be something that was strong before the fire, and STILL strong enough to climb to the top of the church ecosystem's food chain AFTER the fire. so it might not be exactly what we're thinking of. If anyone has good ideas, you get a Bar-cookie if you can reference back to my previous thoughts about being <b><i>influential</i></b>, being <b><i>of the specific area</i></b>, or being <b><i>precise</i></b>.<br /> <br /> 2) Okami -- since its going to be something we hunt, its going to be Dusk that sets it up, so I guess he'll determine the power level. yee ^_^<br /> <br /> 3) Vague spirit ideas:<br /> <br /> Unburnt-Glory - an architecture/building spirit that was generated by the community's love for the building in spite of it being attacked (portfolio: resistance, stone, generosity)<br /> <br /> Shelter-Smoke - a fire/air spirit that coalesced out of the new sort of 'ruined beauty' aesthetic of the church after the attack (portfolio: presence, approporiate element, sanctity)<br /> <br /> Belief-Remains - a spirit that represents the resiliance of faith/spirituality in an otherwise too-cosmopolitan world (portfolio: <b>anti</b>-urban/escapism, communities, belief)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3070,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","user":"Barbrarilen","date":". 03-18-2015, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T10:18:44-07:00","id":447900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/442841-ooc-werewolf-2nd-ed-pbp-ooc-prep-with-dusksage-co?p=447724#post447724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, okay. A couple of thoughts:<br /> <br /> --- oaths and bans with a church are going to be tricky. depending on the actual spirit - it could be a faith spirit, a building/architecture spirit, a community spirit... generally speaking I think we're thinking of 'whatever the ruling spirit over the place is' -- and that means it has to be something that was strong before the fire, and STILL strong enough to climb to the top of the church ecosystem's food chain AFTER the fire. so it might not be exactly what we're thinking of. If anyone has good ideas, you get a Bar-cookie if you can reference back to my previous thoughts about being <b><i>influential</i></b>, being <b><i>of the specific area</i></b>, or being <b><i>precise</i></b>.</div> </div> </div> </div><b><b>\u0ca0_\u0ca0</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">CHALLENGE ACCEPTED<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">Along the old waterfront (I just realized this area is totally not taken guys, voting we set-up shop) </span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">Seas-Luck - A spirit that first came about in the early last century as blue-collar sailors and dockworkers found themselves put out of work. When Prohibition came down they took a personal affront to the law and saw a way to make good money at the same time. No one knew the old coves and caves that dotted the coast like them and they quickly set up shop in one such sea cave, the site of a locus, that led almost right to the speakeasy most it was brought to. Right there in that old cave where these felt at home again with the sounds of the water and the smell of salt the spirit was born out of the mixture of emotions from wealth, to trade, to camaraderie but most of all the desire for the sea. Over time as the spirit and the people coming to this little section of waterfront grew the sailors and bar master unknowingly influenced it further as it influenced them. Soon they came to see that sweet drink arriving on the waves as being given almost by the sea itself and the speakeasy ran with the notion, entertaining its customers with &quot;gifts from our old sea nymph&quot;. The people visiting every were mostly locals they all knew each other and were grateful to relax in such troubled times and they made strangers welcome. What agents their were that could have reported it became regulars themselves, let the dangerous mobs in Chicago be rounded up and put behind bars, there little place was no danger to anybody. Soon the spirit found itself rooted in this sense of community.<br /> <br /> Like most good times though these came crashing down. On Black Friday, the day the stock market crashed a terrible storm tore through the area reminding everyone that the sea was not always so kind. This wrath also affected the spirit and as the wealth brought in by the illegal liqueur was closed with the ending of the Prohibition the spirit lashed out, causing the men and women who had been working together for over ten years to split apart. The people left and the speakeasy closed down, becoming another empty husk on a street lined with those begging for work and food. Times changed and the entire coast was renovated in the modern era now the only ways to find the cave are through its mouth into the sea and the old entrance in the forgotten speakeasy that is now just a closed bar. The spirit lingers still, a force to be reckoned with in the shadow despite the times, surviving off the essence from the locus and what little it could get from the people who still came. It is not satisfied however, it desires a community again, it desires yearning for the sea again. A pack of werewolves once would have been a possible threat to keep an eye on, now, however, perhaps they could give the spirit the means to reclaim itself.<br /> <br /> I find the notion of a church really cool as well, and this area I think is awesome, but I also want to leave Indy something pretty unique to explore with her character rather than us use it as a base. I'm also worried about the kind of spirit we would get there, as it will want us to foster its elements, and any spirit associated with fire is a risk. If we really want to keep a church perhaps it could be what the speakeasy was rebuilt to that quickly went under. This way we have a modernish building that wont require massive renovation costs, and with a little exploring we find the one thing every pack needs (a locus) and one hell of a rocking basement. One tiny problem though, there's a resident spirit, and its not in the best of moods. Then again, we need a totem, and this spirit is strong and old. It knows much of the area and how to influence others. Territory, a base, and a totem, is this where our pack can claim its own?</span><span style=\"font-family:arial\"> I dunno, here's my two cents, let me know what you guys think.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1705,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","user":"Okami","date":". 03-18-2015, 01:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T11:08:59-07:00","id":447965,"title":"","content":"You make a fair point about Indy being very connected to the church already. Her father would have moved out of the neighbourhood, or at least moved on to a different area. Either to escape anymore gang reprisal or as a tacit surrendering to the neighbourhood. Maybe it didn't belong to her father at all, he just spearheaded the renovation of a local historical landmark. Like I said, I'm super flexible on the story of the church itself. Though I love the church, but it doesn't have to be the spirit or even the locus so if we want to move another direction count on me to support it. I don't want Indy hogging any spotlight. She'll be obsessed with the church even if it's just a building.<br /> <br /> A couple questions about the city for Dusk when he has the time. Why is the city called Victory city? Is there an important war that was fought here? Was it an important site in the american revolution? Was it founded by someone important?<br /> <br /> I do like the Unburnt Glory idea a lot though. As far as Okami's concern about the elements, sounds like it would be more a spirit of stone and resistance, than a spirit associated with fire. Maybe the building has a reputation for being cursed, as it's burned down every few generations or so, but always brought back stronger than ever. A spirit focused on biding its time to rebuild its strength and it would be willing to bind itself to a pack to help it through those times when its influence is weakest. I like the idea even of it once being a speakeasy. And maybe before even that it was a site for war plans during the revolution, or the town hall. Or something. At various points throughout its history its been important for different reasons. So its a spirit with a lot of pride and influence that is recently been brought low.<br /> <br /> I would also say that Indy would know none of this. She probably could even never have actually explored this thing on the side of the shadow. It's just a place that was once important to her, and her need for territory had her hang around. Maybe she sensed it was special somehow but had no idea.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, though. Sea's Luck is an interesting idea though because it does change our setting from the usual middle of the city type deal. I'm super down to explore the waterfront idea especially. It'd sort of be interesting to be the pack at the edge of town, by the docks, by the water. The pack that has the smell of the sea and fish in their fur, haha. Probably the smallest territory. Sea caves? I grew up exploring sea caves with my brothers so I'm very partial to that sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 03-18-2015, 02:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T11:41:31-07:00","id":448002,"title":"","content":"*leaves a plate of Bar-cookies out for you darn do-goodnicks*<br /> <br /> <br /> I am really more partial to church than sea-cove, but all of this might be moot if Dusk has his own idea for the hunt and is going to surprise us XD But dude! Totems are awesome!<br /> <br /> I don't think a fire spirit would mean we'd need to burn down the church. Keeping a fire burning, burning wood or incense, that sort of thing could certainly be enough - especially because I think we're all in agreement that the church being destroyed was a bad thing... if we went with that I'd say that 'destructive fire' would be a very good bane for the place, considering its history. (unless it was Unburnt Glory going nyah ha ha even if you burn me down I am still beautiful).<br /> <br /> I vote we enjoy these delicious cookies and wait for Dusksage to absorb all the concentrated awesome we left for him, get his input.<br /> <br /> Also I don't mind giving Indy some spotlight if the character's backstory is an inspiration we all rally around ^_- We will have plenty of time in the game ahead to hog it right back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3070,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","user":"Barbrarilen","date":". 03-18-2015, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T12:06:03-07:00","id":448021,"title":"","content":"I personally love the idea of a church for a rebuilding project/base/totem. It gives us a reason in human terms to all be together, offers us good human ties and provides a central focus to the pack in restoring it and revitalising the area around it, plus, dealing with the gangs roaming the area. <br /> <br /> For my werewolf and human NPCs for the pack, I'm going to offer up David Roberts as a human. He works with Akule but unlike Akule, actually possesses decent social skills (and understands the meaning of customer service). <br /> <br /> Aspiration: To take over he butcher shop himself (currently neither him nor Akule own or manage it)<br /> <br /> Dice pools: Preparing meat 3, Business contacts 4, 'diplomacy' 5<br /> <br /> And wolfblood wise, I'm thinking Lisa Yates who's 18, doesn't really trust people and is a thief and pickpocket, who, incidentally, is on the run from the Pure. She doesn't really trust Akule either, but she wound up in the area he worked in, and his protective instincts came into play. If they ever end up getting closer, it may become a big brother/little sister thing, but right now she trusts him because she has to for her own wellbeing. <br /> <br /> Aspirations:<br /> <br /> Get the Pure off her back<br /> Survive to the next night/day.<br /> <br /> Virtue: Patient<br /> Vice: Deceitful<br /> <br /> Strength: 2<br /> Dex: 3<br /> Stam: 1<br /> <br /> Int: 2<br /> Wits: 3<br /> Resolve: 3<br /> <br /> Presence: 1<br /> Manipulation: 3<br /> Composure: 3<br /> <br /> Skills:<br /> <br /> Investigation: 1<br /> Larceny: 3<br /> Stealth: 4<br /> Athletics: 1<br /> Persuasion: 2<br /> Streetwise: 2<br /> Subterfuge: 2<br /> <br /> Tell: Host Ache<br /> <br /> Merits:<br /> <br /> No moon's birth 2<br /> Small framed: 2<br /> Contacts (black market) 1<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T12:20:42-07:00","id":448026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/442841-ooc-werewolf-2nd-ed-pbp-ooc-prep-with-dusksage-co?p=448002#post448002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*leaves a plate of Bar-cookies out for you darn do-goodnicks*<br /> <br /> <br /> I am really more partial to church than sea-cove, but all of this might be moot if Dusk has his own idea for the hunt and is going to surprise us XD But dude! Totems are awesome!</div> </div> </div> </div>*noms cookies*<br /> <br /> No says we can't have both my friend! ^^(see above section in post combining the two) actually, the more I think about it the I really like the notion of this old stone church built with the remains of the buildings that went down in the storm right over top of the speakeasy that closed down. The sea cave would only be if you find the plastered over entrance to the speakeasy (for instance rather than clear it out they built right over it, so all the old furniture and bottles are still there, preserved like a time capsule. I'd call that crazy but I read an article once where that exact situation happened). Then as you explore you find an entrance old tunnel that leads down and in one direction, soon you hear the sound of waves and the smell of salt, then bam, sea-cave. I dunno, I'm all for combining or going for whatever we're after. I have to admit I am partial to the water front idea though, I like to think werewolves will try to grab a piece of nature regardless of were they are.<br /> <br /> I didn't mean to suggest Indy was hogging anything though, far from it! I just wanted to make any cool developments or events that could happen to her character specifically in her church weren't overshadowed by the fact its now the packs base, thus making them pack-centric instead. I'm all for characters having as much opportunity as possible, my mistake if I ever come off otherwise.<br /> <br /> By the by as we wait for Dusk I also have a question. As a finalize Joseph and get ready to post the sheet I'm encountering the issue of he's also a fetish crafter, a rather good one at four dots, but the fetish rite is four dots and we only have two to start with. Not to mention starting with fetish as a merit is no longer a thing. So are we allowed to spend merit dots on rites if we like? Or say small limited fetishes or talens? If not Im happy to keep as is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1705,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","user":"Okami","date":". 03-18-2015, 03:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T12:40:33-07:00","id":448045,"title":"","content":"The book does say you can trade starting merit dots for rite dots. Up to 5 of them can be traded so if you have spare merit dots you can get the fetish rite pretty easily.<br /> <br /> And no, you didn't suggest anything about hogs, haha. I'm just really enjoying the collaboration and want to make sure everyone gets in.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I really like your Wolfblooded pickpocket, Retias. Sounds like a cool addition to the pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 03-18-2015, 03:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T13:35:17-07:00","id":448174,"title":"","content":"I'd also like to add I'm really looking forward to this game getting started. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T14:24:58-07:00","id":448273,"title":"","content":"I would like to save my Wolfblood for now, if that's okay, Dusk. I think once we find a totem and a place to call home we'll end up inflicting the locals with lunacy here or there XD maybe one of them can be adopted by Aliza (or at least by my ability to make a wolfblood, just after the fact).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T16:03:17-07:00","id":448402,"title":"","content":"Hey all, everything's looking pretty good so far. I do have a timetable update though. For the next couple of days I'm going to have family visiting so hopefully we'll have everything finalized around next week. Keep up the collaboration though, you all have strong ideas and it will be a pleasure to use them in the Chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T16:12:09-07:00","id":448430,"title":"","content":"Glad to hear you like it Dusk. Any guidance with totem talk or what not to talk about or dots or stuff? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> don't leeeeave ussss! D:","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T18:01:39-07:00","id":448543,"title":"","content":"I'd say begin conceptually first and once you've succeeded in binding I then go into stats. You might find inspiration based around how the Spirit reacts and what your Pack must do in order to seal the deal. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T20:42:57-07:00","id":448780,"title":"","content":"Finally! The character sheet!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B67Uzq52HKGmZV9mQXhLaG5nVHM/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B67Uzq52HKGmZV9mQXhLaG5nVHM/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B67Uzq52HKGmZV9mQXhLaG5nVHM/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B67Uzq52HKGmZV9mQXhLaG5nVHM/view?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> One note though, as far the the Firstborn Merit is concerned I don't see Joseph necessarily aware of it. I mean how could you be? Its more just something that is for him, like he knows that when he seriously tells someone to ease off to avoid a fight and <i>means</i> it then most of the time people seem to listen. I don't know, narratively it sounds interesting to me, and I like this idea of this young shaman who still needs to go out and learn basic stuff, like how actually bind a spirit to a totem despite already being good at making the physical item. Plus it gives him a good reason to go see our local Bone Shadow pack once they get established. What do you guys think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T04:00:34-07:00","id":448985,"title":"","content":"I like Okami's comprimise of the Church being nearer the waterfront and connected to these tunnels. Especially because Violet will, at some point take both the cunning and wisdom facets of the Shaping gift, so we can expand and reinforce those tunnels into a killing ground maze as well as a safe place for death rages.<br /> <br /> I edited my wolf blooded into my previous post, here's Grace's sheet and background: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B-UkBhXlxCQZSjlOdUJCM1F3dms/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B-U...ew?usp=sharing</a><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B-UkBhXlxCQZcHV4VldKTHVFd3c/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B-UkBhXlxCQZcHV4VldKTHVFd3c/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B-UkBhXlxCQZcHV4VldKTHVFd3c/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B-UkBhXlxCQZcHV4VldKTHVFd3c/view?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5337-soonmot","name":"soonmot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5337_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T09:31:55-07:00","id":449370,"title":"","content":"ok, so we combine the two?<br /> <br /> How about the church is 'inland' in the waterfront district, so our territory includes the shore but that doesn't mean it has to be right on the water?<br /> <br /> alternatively a 'resisting destruction' theme kind of continues if the church was built hardy enough to weather the wear and tear of being on the water all the time....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T10:13:02-07:00","id":449440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/442841-ooc-werewolf-2nd-ed-pbp-ooc-prep-with-dusksage-co?p=449370#post449370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ok, so we combine the two?<br /> <br /> How about the church is 'inland' in the waterfront district, so our territory includes the shore but that doesn't mean it has to be right on the water?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that's what I was talking about, I'll try to clarify. So what I'm thinking is we have this sea spirit described above, now the church is on say this hill at the end of a street. Down this steep hill is the rock shore and the hill itself melds into cliffs on one side. Now there's a sea cave in a cove in these cliffs but no way to get to it except water, that's where the church comes in. It was built on this speakeasy (or what have you, again, we can change this how we want) which had a secret tunnel connecting it to the cave in order to bring in illegal goods (I chose prohibition because it would have allowed for the development of an influential spirit of the sort we want without necessarily being attached to a gang or larger crime). In this cave is a loci that hasnt been claimed precisely because of it being hidden, while scouting for territory our pack could want to claim the waterfront area which currently has no pack, while looking for potential loci (which every pack needs we investigate the church and notice it seems like a likely site (I'll need to look up just how one could detect a locus). Only problem is there's an old rather powerful spirit that's rather defensive of the place. Luckily we need a totem, and there's an old rater powerful spirit that's rather defensive of the place. Eh? Eh? ;D.<br /> <br /> Oh, and by the end of street i don't necessarily mean by itself, which we could do if we wanted, but at the end of a street with shops or apartments since the docks are nearby.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1705,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","user":"Okami","date":". 03-19-2015, 01:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T10:37:00-07:00","id":449459,"title":"","content":"Sorry Okami, your descriptions are just a little erratic. The rest of the group had seemed to be on board with the spirit being <i>of</i> the church (Indy had a connection to it, I liked it being tied to a concrete single spot) and your counter was a sea-spirit which kind of came out of left field?<br /> <br /> If I'm reading your idea correctly, you want us to potentially have a locus in the caves down by the water, instead of a locus at the church?<br /> <br /> The caves might be an area full of emotional resonance because of the history (old spot), tradition of secrets (prohibition bootlegging), familiarity (known only by 'the locals')... but a place that feeds off privacy is eventually going to be forgotten, isn't it? I don't know if it would be very strong if people don't know about it anymore. That would make it pretty dangerous, if it is a once-powerful area that's now pretty starved for essence because its nearly forgotten?<br /> <br /> Ignoring that for the moment, if we were to say, have our totem be the spirit of the ruined church, and the whole area was our headquarters, and from the church we just happen to have the easiest access to the locus down by the water because of tunnels running between them, that sounds to me like a good combination of everyone's ideas so far?<br /> <br /> I don't really want us to be thinking up the encounters - that's Dusk's job - if there <i>are</i> sea spirits, we'll just show some fang and remind them who's the alpha predator in this area, eh? : D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T10:38:44-07:00","id":449462,"title":"","content":"Having it in an older, poorer section of the city works well for me. It's a low income, blue collar area, mostly dockworkers, fishermen, and the owners of small, struggling local shops. Of course, since it's waterfront, or near waterfront, there's outside pressure to purchase the real estate, tear down the history and rebuild as high priced condos and big box stores, chasing out the people who traditionally live there in favor of the rich. None of our characters have many dots in resources, so a bit of class struggle can add another dimension to the hunt and the way we tend our territory.<br /> <br /> Maybe the gang that burned down the church was getting paid by a development firm? Maybe we have to contend with spirits of greed spreading their influence.<br /> <br /> I'm going to try and nap, I'll have the human pack member for Violet up tonight as well as a traditional background for her. Hopefully I'll write about her meeting with her vampire frenemy, but comic books and netflix may prevent that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5337-soonmot","name":"soonmot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5337_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T10:56:58-07:00","id":449475,"title":"","content":"I'm fairly happy to go with the majority on this, and the church connected o the cove by old tunnels we can explore, dig out and reinforce works very well for me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T11:33:30-07:00","id":449494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/442841-ooc-werewolf-2nd-ed-pbp-ooc-prep-with-dusksage-co?p=449459#post449459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry Okami, your descriptions are just a little erratic. The rest of the group had seemed to be on board with the spirit being <i>of</i> the church (Indy had a connection to it, I liked it being tied to a concrete single spot) and your counter was a sea-spirit which kind of came out of left field?<br /> <br /> If I'm reading your idea correctly, you want us to potentially have a locus in the caves down by the water, instead of a locus at the church?</div> </div> </div> </div>I see how I could have come across that way, and I apologize. I should clarify how I've been going about the discussion.<br /> <br /> Ok, So back when I first posted about the spirit and the new location it was more in response to your post on page three that mentioned we should discuss the kinds of spirits we could consider as a totem and what we want out of them. Then the discussion of Indy's church and its spirit came along and while I thought it was cool I also saw it as the first proposed option in a discussion about possible spirits.<br /> <br /> As I thought about what kinds of spirits we could go for in a totem I thought having something a little bit nature-y would be cool too, as I like the notion of werewolves being kind of pulled towards nature when they come across it (even in a city) because its natural to them. This led me to peruse through Dusk's posting of the sections of the city and how the territory was carved up and I noticed that as a coastal city the waterfront hadn't been taken up. I thought this would be a cool way to combine the urban and the natural. That led me to wondering about 'ok, if we change settings from in the city with this old church to the waterfront, what might that do to what spirits we could find around?'<br /> <br /> My head was already liking the idea of this history you guys really liked with the church, the idea of it being old right? So then I got thinking about cities on the coast a hundred years or so ago, and remembered this documentary I has seen about fishermen who turned to bootlegging alcohol. They used the local sea caves and even made tunnels connecting each other's homes (as all the homes were wall to wall where they lived. Pretty much everybody knew about it from what I could recollect, but even if they didn't my head was aware of how back then sometimes whole towns would be in on it). I began to wonder what kind of spirit might grow out of that, so that's where all of that came from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/442841-ooc-werewolf-2nd-ed-pbp-ooc-prep-with-dusksage-co?p=449459#post449459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The caves might be an area full of emotional resonance because of the history (old spot), tradition of secrets (prohibition bootlegging), familiarity (known only by 'the locals')... but a place that feeds off privacy is eventually going to be forgotten, isn't it? I don't know if it would be very strong if people don't know about it anymore. That would make it pretty dangerous, if it is a once-powerful area that's now pretty starved for essence because its nearly forgotten?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I put in the notion of a church being built over it, the spirit got by through eating the essence the new place generated that was the same as the old, then the new place too ran its course. As I wrote all this down I realized that, as I've studied urban environments in college, its amazing how buildings and neighborhoods we just assume have always been around can radically change from decade to decade and what we think is 'traditional' or 'old' really isnt at all, things are built over, taken apart, and forgotten. That made me suddenly remember an article I read once about how during renovations in a restaurant in a city they found an entire speakeasy, complete with furniture and bottles, just behind an old wall. The place had just been covered up and forgotten. So I never really saw the resonance of much of the essence being truly 'secret'. It was more 'open secret' or what we often simply call 'community'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/442841-ooc-werewolf-2nd-ed-pbp-ooc-prep-with-dusksage-co?p=449459#post449459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ignoring that for the moment, if we were to say, have our totem be the spirit of the ruined church, and the whole area was our headquarters, and from the church we just happen to have the easiest access to the locus down by the water because of tunnels running between them, that sounds to me like a good combination of everyone's ideas so far?</div> </div> </div> </div>We could do that, I'm good with what the pack decides. I apologize if I came across as 'We need to do this instead!' Which I realize I likely did. I just saw the whole thing more as someone tossed this idea out and we stirred it around to see what we liked, rather than actually coming to a decision. So I wanted to throw out another idea so we could stir that around and see what we liked out of it too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/442841-ooc-werewolf-2nd-ed-pbp-ooc-prep-with-dusksage-co?p=449459#post449459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really want us to be thinking up the encounters - that's Dusk's job - if there <i>are</i> sea spirits, we'll just show some fang and remind them who's the alpha predator in this area, eh? : D</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, didnt mean to try and design the encounter, I was really just thinking about how things might happen, but I guess those could be called the same thing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1705,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","user":"Okami","date":". 03-19-2015, 02:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T12:38:30-07:00","id":449581,"title":"","content":"Well what else should we talk about? Connections? How people met? Wolf-blooded &amp; humans? I liked the comment about worse-off economically, blue-collar attitudes to things - and the need to protect the old neighborhood from redevelopment -- all of that stuff definitely resonates with me about what Aliza's past must have been like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T14:01:11-07:00","id":449747,"title":"","content":"For sea caves, there's no reason that there couldn't have been a gold/silver rush in the area in the 1800's, with these tunnels being used to Shanghai drunks into service on sailing ships. So you'd have spirits of faith and community from the church, spirits of fire and destruction from it's burning in the building proper. Some of revelry, passion, and intoxication from the time as a speakeasy still holding on in the tunnels that were used for the hidden bar area and then, deeper in and slumbering forgotten, these nasty spirits of terror and fear left over from people being kidnapped as crew or human cargo for far off ports.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5337-soonmot","name":"soonmot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5337_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T14:36:39-07:00","id":449774,"title":"","content":"Hmm... I imagine Joseph joining last, being new to town. In terms of wolf-blooded and humans I'll hold off on that till after the totem. Joseph has some people he could contact but he'll need a catalyst to actually make the move.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T14:59:46-07:00","id":449801,"title":"","content":"Aliza was born and raised here. I'm playing with the idea of her human or her wolfblood being family that's also in town to help strengthen how much a part of the community she is. Depending on ST's desires, she may be just-familiar-with the neighborhood or literally brought up in it. Depending on how big the town is there's still a decent chance she and the other locals don't know each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T18:42:54-07:00","id":450007,"title":"","content":"Oh wow. I've missed a lot here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T18:45:40-07:00","id":450008,"title":"","content":"About the debate of the church and the speakeasy. How about this? A spirit of resistance or community or safehaven is at the heart of all this. The caves were heavily influential in the founding of the city, many of the founders made their fortune mining the gold deposits in those caves, and the building above it may have been the original town hall of Victory City. It was a city formed of wealth and cooperation. This formed a powerful spirit of community.<br /> <br /> As the city grew however, the building was too small and not central enough in location and eventually fell out of use. However, later during the prohibition, the spirit's influence came into play again. Being one of the poorest blue-collar neighbourhoods in the city, prohibition hit this area pretty hard. The community was in need for a place where workers who needed to unwind or let loose or unburden themselves in. So the spirit's influence was behind the speakeasy that formed in the caves underneath the building. It was important in reviving the spirits of this worn down community. Until it was found and shut down.<br /> <br /> Many years later, as crime and gang violence in the neighbourhood reached an all time high, the community grew afraid to leave their homes. The spirit's influence came into play again. The building was purchased and renovated into a church, and that church became a beacon of light in neighbourhood that might have succumbed to the bleakness of its situation. The community took a stand against the violence, they banded together and slowly the influence of the gangs in the area diminished. Until the church was burned down. <br /> <br /> And here we are. So we have a spirit that is very old, and has been looking after this area for centuries. Very influential. Would definitely have an impact on how we run the pack, and sort of combines all the bases so far. The locus itself could be in the recently burned down church, or further down in the caves, a dimming locus somehow still alive and resonant for all these years.<br /> <br /> So the spirit could be of the building itself, or just a spirit of Community or Rebirth/Renewal or Resistance. Could be called something like Safehaven. Though each time the spirit does something for the community, it seems to be foiled so it could even have a rival spirit. A spirit formed at the same time (gold mining, founding the city) of Greed or Corruption, one of the few spirits with more influence in the town.<br /> <br /> Okay, now I'm sort going into Storyteller territory so I'll back off. I don't know. Just trying to find a neat middle for all the great ideas we're all coming up with. We have a combination of the urban and the natural. We have a blue-collar, working-class community by the sea/docks, with fishermen and small shops, that is beset with crime and a potential target for redevelopment goals that we may have to thwart. Yea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T19:12:04-07:00","id":450023,"title":"","content":"As far as meetings and connections:<br /> <br /> <br /> Indy would be a local girl as well. Probably hanging around the remains of the church with no idea of how important the site really was. I'd think whoever came up with the bright idea of starting a pack (I'm think Aliza right now, since I can't imagine it being Indy, since Akule is so young, Violet is a new and hesitant member of the pack, and Joseph is new to the city in general) probably came across Indy first. Being the pack mom puts Aliza in the position of being the easy starting point for the pack, even if she isn't a leader in the strictest sense. Akule is relatively new moved to the city, but if he got a job at the butchery nearby in town, he'd be an easy meeting to imagine. Seems like he is looking to start over after the stuff with his Uncle and so it wouldn't be a hard sell for the pack mom to make to the youngster.<br /> <br /> Then there's Violet or Joseph. I'm thinking Indy and Violet could even have a very distant connection of having gone to school together. Not as friends or anything, but as &quot;that weird/quiet/whatever girl i passed in the halls sometimes.&quot;<br /> <br /> And that recognition could have sparked the initial introduction to the pack. Just a &quot;hey, don't I know you...&quot;<br /> <br /> Just throwing out ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T19:30:49-07:00","id":450030,"title":"","content":"It kind of sounds like we like smashing all the ideas we've had together, then. I'm cool with a spirit of community.<br /> <br /> How do we feel about remodeling the ex-church as a pub? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I think we could make the spirit <b>HELLA </b>happy to see the town coming together again (for a pint). I could also make that Aliza's past - I have more merit dots to spend, I could give her some resources/background in bartending, it could be what her family did that she was trying to get out of with the library-stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3070,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","user":"Barbrarilen","date":". 03-19-2015, 10:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T19:58:19-07:00","id":450037,"title":"","content":"Amravanti, you literally get all of the internets, and my yeses to plan smash-everything-together. Now we just need to hard-iron out the stats of the spirit provided everyone's good with is idea. What say ye fellow players? Also Barb we definitely need to do this renovation. As it turns out there's a former singer in the pack who could pull some threads if he ever decides to call up some old friends... (guess I know where my early experiences are going) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1705,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","user":"Okami","date":". 03-19-2015, 11:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T22:39:19-07:00","id":450170,"title":"","content":"Haha. I aim to please. I'm down for us making some renovations to the old church. Sounds great. Could totally be part of the deal we make with the spirit or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T23:14:36-07:00","id":450196,"title":"","content":"I'm on board with everything Amravanti posted and love the idea of turning the burnt out ruins into a bar. Less suspicious to be constantly hanging out there than in a rebuilt church. <br /> <br /> My advice when making wolf-blooded, as they're almost as important as our actual characters: Use them to shore up our weaknesses. I made Grace into a negotiator of sorts, that way Aliza has some backup. Having one or two more fighty to help Akule, especially with the regeneration or dalu/ urshal transformation tells would probably be nice.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5337-soonmot","name":"soonmot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5337_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T23:20:35-07:00","id":450197,"title":"","content":"Hi gang, very pleased to see the collaboration coming along so swimmingly. The only thin I feel like addressing is the early mention by Okami that Werewolves are drawn to nature. That's somewhat of a fallacy in regards to the Uratha since the Hisil supposedly encompasses all the known universe, and that included manmade cities. The encroachment of man is drastically changing the spiritual landscape in the same way that metropolitan cities changed the social landscape for humanity. The reason Werewolves feel drawn to nature is because the Spirit half of them is a spirit of The Hunt and are naturally drawn to any location where The Hunt has the strongest resonance.<br /> <br /> That was more of a nitpick by me than anything though. Please continue crafting and collaboration. Your ideas are making Victory City come to life before my eyes and it's amazing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T02:48:11-07:00","id":450263,"title":"","content":"I made this so we can pool our Pack and City into one page. Please let me know if you can't modify the page with this link and I'll work something out.<br /> <br /> (Please personal message me if you don't have the google doc favorited.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":") 04-03-2015, 03:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T09:46:22-07:00","id":450534,"title":"","content":"Added the latest thought on Totem, made some additions to it, and c&amp;p'd all mentioned pack relations. Edit those if you think your ideas have changed as we talk. Also pretty sure there's a difference between pack relations and pack connections --- if there's anything you want to add about elders recently giving people orders or blessings or shuffling us around that would bring us together, Dusk, let us know, and then I'll start a discussion for us to go hog-wild saying 'well so and so met so and so here' so you have more hooks to play with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3070,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","user":"Barbrarilen","date":". 03-20-2015, 01:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T13:24:51-07:00","id":450791,"title":"","content":"There we go, made my own additions to the document. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T13:59:31-07:00","id":450838,"title":"","content":"Oh, good idea Retias. Added my human and wolfblood too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T21:14:40-07:00","id":451279,"title":"","content":"added to the totem talk and a few lines here and there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T08:54:59-07:00","id":451577,"title":"","content":"Sorry I've been out of contact, last few days have been busier than I anticipated. I'll finish my stuff this weekend <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5337-soonmot","name":"soonmot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5337_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T18:20:54-07:00","id":452198,"title":"","content":"Just checking up on the Doc and MAN you guy's have made that indespencable. Excellent job everyone, I'll be hopefully updating the Doc with more story points soon. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T01:35:24-07:00","id":453966,"title":"","content":"So I've started working on a wolfblooded character in an attempt to bolster our combat capability as soonmot suggested.<br /> <br /> This is my idea so far.<br /> <br /> Character Sheet: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BxK0La5plUm8UjUzczJsNXpKZ1E/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BxK...ew?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> His/her name is Teller Stone. Teller comes from a long line of Blood Talons and her family was respected within the tribe. She's the daughter of a Blood Talon named Markos 'Blackheart', a renowned warrior who infamously went mad one day and murdered his entire pack. Soon after, he defected to the Predator Kings. In the years that followed, he led a pack of the Pure on a killing spree of almost unprecedented proportions.all across the West Coast. No one knows why he changed allegiances so suddenly. For years 'Blackheart' became something of a bogeyman among the People. A terror that could show up in your territory and slowly take your pack apart piece by piece. Eventually Markos and his pack were hunted down and killed by a group of his former tribemates, but none of them have ever forgotten the depths of his madness and his treachery.<br /> <br /> Teller lives her life trying to escape the shadow of her father's legacy. She had idolized her father. He was everything she wanted to be. Now she has to distance herself from his name and his memory, or be shunned by her people. She took her mother's last name, Stone, and she's been trying to outrun her father's name ever since.<br /> <br /> Teller is young, but she's been in a pack since she was 16. She's basically a born and raised werewolf, and has been groomed her whole life to be a Blood Talon. She's trained to fight with Silver weaponry. Trained in various combat tactics. She's basically a soldier. Her first change hasn't come yet, but she's sure it's just a matter of time. Even if it doesn't, she's not going to let that get in the way of her goal to rewrite her family's legacy.<br /> <br /> So Teller has something to prove to not just the world, but herself. She's looking to start over because she hates the scrutiny and stigma that follows her around, especially with Blood Talons. She moved to this part of the state in particular because it doesn't have a very heavy Blood Talon presence. She treasures her chance friendship with Indiana because it's the first relationship she ever made with someone who had never even heard of her father. It's the first relationship she's had without that judgement and suspicion. Even more, when she eventually told Indy about her father's history, Indy did not care. She didn't even understand why anyone would judge Teller for her father's sins. No one suspected Indiana might be a Protestant Minister just because her father was. Why should Teller be treated any differently? Because of this Teller is very grateful, and because of that she has decided that this is where she'll finally settle down and start over. <br /> <br /> She's going to have either the Liar's Skin, Second Skin or Anger Issues Tells. Not sure yet. Her gender is also undetermined, I've just been using female pronouns as a placeholder. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T05:19:17-07:00","id":454111,"title":"","content":"Teller sounds awesome! To be honest I still feel weird about making wolfblooded - kind of like how in a game of d&amp;d if you aren't careful the pet or the mount can outshine one of the other players? I am glad you're making a strong one, makes me feel more confident about my choice (who might be a decent front man to run the bar!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T06:39:53-07:00","id":454184,"title":"","content":"I agree, great job, she sounds like a great addition to the pack. She adds a great depth this Pure and Forsaken conflict that has happened recently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T07:02:32-07:00","id":454224,"title":"","content":"That was one of the nicer things in the new edition, sometimes you play as your wolf blooded! I'd totally play as Grace in a different game, she's a fun character with great ambitions.<br /> <br /> I love Teller! Running from an unwanted past but trying to live up to a legacy of glory, great character!<br /> <br /> (I am currently typing up Violet's background and my human pack member)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B-UkBhXlxCQZR0pUcE9CbFV5ODg/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B-U...ew?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> Derek Pope: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B-UkBhXlxCQZS1ltNk1USktGeEE/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B-U...ew?usp=sharing</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5337,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5337-soonmot","user":"soonmot","date":". 03-23-2015, 11:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5337-soonmot","name":"soonmot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5337_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T13:26:04-07:00","id":454793,"title":"","content":"While we are adding things, can we get other voices weighing in on totem talk? Okami and I are going at it like two dogs with one bone between us, fresh perspectives would be quite welcome! ^.^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T14:32:51-07:00","id":454852,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I tried to make a wolf blooded character that I would be excited to play. I'm glad you all like her. And hey, if we need a bouncer or security for the bar, we have it. She's pretty tough.<br /> <br /> Not sure if I have any human beings to offer to the pack. I was thinking Indy has a younger sibling and maybe a friend or two at the dog groomer's, but none of them seem like they'd have much to offer the pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T23:57:04-07:00","id":455496,"title":"","content":"You two are handling totem talk so well I reallyhave nothing to add. Things that have resonated with me: The burnedout church has a long, long history in Victory City. It was most recently a church, but before that it wasthe1920's speakeasy. In the mid 1800's it wasa boardinghousefor sailors wherepeople were kidnapped. Before American expansion, the tunnels were a holy place for native tribes,maybe spot for rituals or burials of important heroes.<br /> <br /> That spirit isn't something of faith, or booze, or even the sea, but of Perserverance. Something that can get knocked down again and again (and maybe it keeps getting knocked down because it has an opposite spirit who wars against it) but always gets back up and rebuilds. That an important part of the spirit is that it fosters a sense of community. Whatever it rebuilds as is always a gathering place. Having the pack there to guard against it's inevitable destruction is a big win for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5337-soonmot","name":"soonmot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5337_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T23:58:20-07:00","id":455497,"title":"","content":"EDIT: I'm sure human members will come as we RP, we need bartenders, servers, bouncers. People who will be &quot;ours&quot; but probably not in on the secret.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5337-soonmot","name":"soonmot","avatar":"https://foru