152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T08:27:32-07:00","id":460029,"title":"","content":"So did I, truth be told. :S","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T09:07:53-07:00","id":460064,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the bar was going to be called the apple tree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5337-soonmot","name":"soonmot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5337_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T09:26:36-07:00","id":460086,"title":"","content":"The spirit is going to be a name of Perseverence! Like... uhm.. (apparently longer more complex names denote more powerful spirits, so it should just be like, a two-word epitaph) ...<br /> <br /> Still-Standing<br /> Ever-Bright<br /> Indefatigable<br /> Soon-Victory (considering the city we're in)<br /> <br /> <br /> If we adopt a /new/ spirit that's as much one of 'our renewing the church as the bar' because of the resonance of the area so of COURSE new spirits would happily form because of our actions ... then yea it might be perseverence-through-revelry/alcohol/adaptation ... but it'd also be a more specific spirit and I think by nature a weaker one?<br /> <br /> I'm sure once our spirit gets more influential, though, our bar is just going to get more and more popular and integral with the community. PREPARE TO PUT DOTS IN RESOURCES! WE'RE GONNA BE RICH! : D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3070,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","user":"Barbrarilen","date":". 03-28-2015, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T14:25:53-07:00","id":460417,"title":"","content":"Ah, nvm. I misread the conversation earlier. The apple tree is a fine name for a bar. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also if anyone has a good link to a good rules layout for play by post please post it in the chat. There might have been one posted up earlier but I can't remember.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  A bit of laziness on my part. - . -' 03-28-2015, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T20:03:16-07:00","id":460622,"title":"","content":"Dusk, I looked at your post like 5x and still don't know what you mean. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T21:13:32-07:00","id":460653,"title":"","content":"Ah, I was wondering if anyone had a website link to a decent explanation of the rules for a Play by Post Chronicle. I wrote that when I first woke up so it came across as a little garbled. - . -'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T23:55:31-07:00","id":460775,"title":"","content":"I think it's simply a case of taking it a step at a time if you're new to play by post running. Set an initial scene, see how things start and adjusrt. The advantage s, you have lots of time to check things before you put a post up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T00:11:11-07:00","id":460788,"title":"","content":"Ah ok, that sounds a lot simpler than I thought. Thanks Retias.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T09:52:17-07:00","id":461110,"title":"","content":"We can set a post order, and I would recommend there's a window before we skip you. Like, post at least once every 48 hours, or not hard feelings when we go past you and catch up where its appropriate.<br /> <br /> Also for consistency things like how we post rolls, where we roll, when we use quote/spoiler boxes, when we use color.... Are italics for internal monolgues... Little stuff like that just looks better if we are consistent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T12:40:10-07:00","id":461353,"title":"","content":"I like it. Thanks for the advice Barbrarilen. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T19:03:32-07:00","id":461749,"title":"","content":"Agreed, also Dusk there's a thread on the forums here about how to run a pbp game. Browsed through it a while ago and thought it was super helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T20:49:54-07:00","id":461834,"title":"","content":"Sweet, that's what I was hoping for. Do you remember what the thread was called?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck. 03-29-2015, 11:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T04:44:26-07:00","id":462097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/423517-how-to-gm-a-pbp-game\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/423517-how-to-gm-a-pbp-game\"> How to GM a PBP game? - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/423517-how-to-gm-a-pbp-game\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/423517-how-to-gm-a-pbp-game </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Somewhat what the title says. Exalted 2E is the game I'm looking to run, but I've never run a game before. I'm not sure if it would be a lost cause for me to try, as I've also never played Exalted or even a tabletop RPG. I've taken extensive notes of the relevant sections and have most of the sourcebooks. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T07:40:42-07:00","id":462239,"title":"","content":"Here's what I do: Write out a general outline of what the main plot is going to be. Don't get too detailed, because players <s>ruin everything!</s> will surprise you with their inventiveness. <br /> <br /> Make a list of important clues or character beats that will forward your main as well as a few important NPCs. Look for opportunities to insert these clues or NPCs or events into the crazy scenes your players end up in. What this does is two very important things. #1 it keeps the game heading in the direction you've written for it while #2 allowing the players to actually push the plot forward through their actions instead of railroading.<br /> <br /> <br /> The good news is that PBP is so much slower than IRL games, so you actually have time to sit back and think about how to spin our actions into plot gold instead of having to improvise on the fly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5337-soonmot","name":"soonmot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5337_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T08:42:56-07:00","id":462327,"title":"","content":"So very, very slow. Q.Q","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T18:24:12-07:00","id":462968,"title":"","content":"But good things come to those who wait my friend. We shall spin a tale for the ages!<br /> <br /> Oh, and when it comes to a Totem name, last time I checked we were settling on a spirit of Perseverance? In that case I think Ever-Bright sounds great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1705,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","user":"Okami","date":". 03-31-2015, 08:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T07:54:43-07:00","id":463564,"title":"","content":"It was just an idea. Whatever we name it, what would it look like in Hisil, I wonder?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T10:07:27-07:00","id":463628,"title":"","content":"I have no idea, the idea of spirits looking like something singular and definite, like an owl or a tree and representing something more, is so ingrained in me that I have a hard time thinking of what a spirit that is a concept would look like if it wasn't one of those things. Maybe its a pool of what looks like liquid? Water or something? The only reason I say that is something like stone feels too cliche to me. Stone doesn't really persevere, water wears it away and cracks it (especially the sandstone of the waterfront I imagine), chemicals eat it. Something like a pool or the ocean is always there, changeless, unless you fill it in (in the case of say a pond) You can pollute it sure, but no matter what you can't get rid of it. I dunno, will wrack my brain on it for a while.<br /> <br /> Edit: Actually, given that it was a church recently that might have affected its appearance, like maybe its a constantly overflowing spring or something. Water of Life and all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T15:18:42-07:00","id":463925,"title":"","content":"Given the closeness to the sea, I would not be opposed to some juxtaposition. A glowing ball of mortar that roils in place like the tides? :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T15:21:26-07:00","id":463926,"title":"","content":"How about a stone tortoise with a spring or fountain flowing from its back? Maybe the water that spills over glows or rejuvenates? Preferably salt water.<br /> <br /> Don't know if Ever-Bright works as a name for that necessarily, just throwing out an idea.<br /> <br /> Maybe its made of limestone, since limestone is sedimentary and usually oceanside. Or it could look like Ethiopian Welo Opal, since that's a stone that looks like the ocean, though I think it's metamorphic and not usually found near the ocean at all.<br /> <br /> Edit: Welo opal looks like <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/lmmvlUV.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>. <br /> <br /> And it turns out opals are mineraloids and not metamorphic at all, so it would make sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":".  Picture of welo opal. 03-31-2015, 06:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T15:35:07-07:00","id":463950,"title":"","content":"ok, i love the tortoise with a fountain on its back idea. I'd totally love to go with that, or something similar, we could even have it have some plants or something on there as well for the whole rejuvenation aspect since it keeps coming back as well as persevering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T15:36:32-07:00","id":463951,"title":"","content":"Though you make a good point about stone, it does erode. We could have it's own water function differently and strengthen rather than eroded things. Definitely like the idea of having plants (even though that wouldn't normally happen with salt water) and stuff growing on it. Even if it's just lichen or moss or something.<br /> <br /> Edit: Obviously it also doesn't even have to be made of stone, of course. That did not occur to me. It can be fresh water too of course, in which case any plants are fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 03-31-2015, 06:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T19:12:52-07:00","id":464166,"title":"","content":"It isn't natural preservation though, its human preservation. I wouldn't have it doing the plant/nature thing because we're talking more societal urban local rejuvenation and resiliance.<br /> <br /> What if it was made up of the reincarnations of the area? Like the shell was stained glass from the church, and so forth?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T19:56:16-07:00","id":464198,"title":"","content":"So basically our spirit will look like bulbasaur <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> edit: (I really do like the tortoise with a fountain and growing life on it's back.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5337-soonmot","name":"soonmot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5337_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T04:58:08-07:00","id":464564,"title":"","content":"Bulbasaur is my favorite starter. &gt;.&gt;<br /> <br /> What if Victory City's flag has a frog/turtle on it? This is, in essence, a minor (minor minor junior minor) piece of the spirit of the city, after all.<br /> <br /> Gonna totally repeat that it should have a non-organic feel to it, though :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T05:32:14-07:00","id":464599,"title":"","content":"I could see it being made of stained glass as pretty cool, though I'm ok with the organic feel. I don't think it really matters for spirits where the essence comes from, human or not, what matters most is its resonance (at least in my mind). Though I only mean that for a spirit like ours which is inherently abstract, obviously the spirit of a fox or wolf or tree will be as its namesake with some adjustments. So I don't think its necessary for one feel or the other, at this point I think its more aesthetics that should be somewhat relevant. So, we seem to like the bulbasaur look (woot), and I'm good with either the inorganic or organic-<br /> <br /> Wait. what if we combine the two, like its the tortoise with a fountain and garden on its back but the fruit or flowers of the plant are stained glass? That sounds awesome to me. If there were spirit beauty competitions ours would totally win at this rate. &gt;.&gt;<br /> <br /> And the plants that grow could have symbolic meaning for rejuvenation or perseverance. To Google!<br /> <br /> So, not finding much that really accentuates what we're going for, so I'm gonna put a vote in for a grass lily styled one. For reasons, and glorious glorious Metal Gear references.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1705,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","user":"Okami","date":".  After some quick searching... 04-01-2015, 08:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T11:19:36-07:00","id":464911,"title":"","content":"Hey gang, again love the collaboration talks. Just want to interject that the Victory City flag's animal is actually an eagle. Mostly because another Pack already had the same ideas you guys did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T11:34:47-07:00","id":464924,"title":"","content":"Ooh shut down <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Perseverance because of tortoise- and-the-hare, then?<br /> <br /> I would like something more abstract than an animal to be honest. I am just stuck on stained glass, now. Dusk, do you have an impression or some input on what the spirits might be/inhabit our storied building of choice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3070,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","user":"Barbrarilen","date":". 04-01-2015, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T12:04:49-07:00","id":464948,"title":"","content":"Couldn't the church itself have a spirit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T12:33:45-07:00","id":464970,"title":"","content":"No reason why it shouldn't...unless there is a reason. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (There's no reason.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Lolz 04-01-2015, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T13:05:36-07:00","id":465061,"title":"","content":"Well the building. It ain't a church anymore. And I kind of thought that was the idea - the spirit of the building, with a resonance of perseverance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T13:06:38-07:00","id":465064,"title":"","content":"As for Barbrarilen's question all I'd have to say is that Spirit's appearance can range anywhere from the fantastic to the surreal. There's no reason that it can't really be a fusion of all of the above if you want, so long as it symbolically reflects it nature or just looks too damn cool. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Take for instance the Totem of the Whisper Catchers: Listening Wind, an entity invisible except outside of the Hisil since it appears to be made entirely out of wind except for two glowing eyes that seem to be set I to a vaguely humanoid head. The spirit resembles a lanky chimpanzee with it's elongated arms but lacks a tail. It speaks by touching an individual, who then hears the entity whisper within their ear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":". 04-01-2015, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T00:59:22-07:00","id":467112,"title":"","content":"The Warden Moon rises over Victory City,<br /> <br /> Her chosen howl in revelry and stalk the men, spirits, and rat Hosts that lurk where her light doesn't shine.<br /> <br /> His enemies howl in rage and stalk her chosen servants, be they men, spirits, or Uratha like themselves but Forsaken in heart and soul.<br /> <br /> Tonight the Hunt begins, but who will be the prey? A new predator walks through the darkness of Victory, and within it's eyes lies a secret pain that is the byproduct of the Warden Moon and here rage filled children. Will he sit there and let her flesh and blood suffer for his own mercurial whims? Or will the cries for salvation of both Forsaken and Pure alike fall to the ears of such a cold and distant light?<br /> <br /> Let's find out shall we?<br /> <br /> For one way or another...the wolf must hunt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/467118-ic-the-wolves-of-victory-dusksage-s-pbp-werewolf-the-forsaken-2e-chronicle\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/467118-ic-the-wolves-of-victory-dusksage-s-pbp-werewolf-the-forsaken-2e-chronicle\"> IC The Wolves of Victory: Dusksage's PbP Werewolf the Forsaken 2E Chronicle - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/467118-ic-the-wolves-of-victory-dusksage-s-pbp-werewolf-the-forsaken-2e-chronicle\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/467118-ic-the-wolves-of-victory-dusksage-s-pbp-werewolf-the-forsaken-2e-chronicle </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The Hunt begins now! Our troupe's cast will consist of: Myself (Dusksage) as the ST and secret True Fae puppeterng these foolish mortals to their doom ;) Soonmoot as Violet Caravell, the Farsil Luhal Irraka Amravanti as Indiana Annan, the Meninna Irraka Okami as Joseph Christensen, the Hirfathra Hissu </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  And so it begins... 04-03-2015, 04:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T14:50:03-07:00","id":467888,"title":"","content":"A couple of quick things before I head off to the IC. I'm cool with just posting my character's backstory, but I'm curious, would you guys prefer I do that or reveal it through play? Also, updated character sheets.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B67Uzq52HKGmYmhqeTgxQ2NFUzQ/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B67Uzq52HKGmYmhqeTgxQ2NFUzQ/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B67Uzq52HKGmYmhqeTgxQ2NFUzQ/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B67Uzq52HKGmYmhqeTgxQ2NFUzQ/view?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Also, on the totem talk, we seem pretty set on our tortoise fountain bro, unless we want to hash it out some more which I'm also cool with. I know Barb's wanting to consider some more abstract designs. That said, I don't know if we ever decided on how strong we think it will be (do we decide that or do you Dusksage? I don't want to step on any toes).<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm all for the notion of a baby jaggling. This thing is a tough ombre to be taken down only to come back so many times, but I don't see it as in the height of its power right now due to the church collapsing. Jaggling is the level at which spirits actually become involved in politics rather than on pure survival, so I could see it having some influence on the local area but that's it. Strictly a lesser for sure in my mind. I know we'll need to invest exp into it to determine its actual mechanical strength, but I like to imagine this as more of its 'roleplay' strength, what do you all think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1705,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","user":"Okami","date":". 04-07-2015, 10:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T15:34:08-07:00","id":467915,"title":"","content":"Well I'm not sure, actually. Are we already a pack? It's sounding like we aren't. Are roleplaying from the point where your character comes into town, for example? It all depends on how early into our pack's forming we are beginning. Can I ask for a little more direction, O' Mighty ST?<br /> <br /> I definitely like the tortoise fountain a lot. I'm also not averse to it having more modern traits derived from the influences its had on the area. (Stained glass for the shell, for example). And I'm down with a lesser jaggling if we can manage it, the rank isn't too important to me. None of the abstract designs so far really struck me, but I'm willing to go with one if there's something the group really likes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T16:05:36-07:00","id":467931,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the input. I was under the impression we were a just-formed pack in the IC, so I translated Retias's post as backstory type stuff, since Dusk asked for some. I thought we'd be jumping in just were we leave off here, discovering this awesome base with a spirit we can hunt for a totem, and getting to know each other in the mean time. I would also like some ST clarification if we can have it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T18:24:50-07:00","id":468056,"title":"","content":"I would think a start pf 'we're just being put together right now' like this is our first meeting makes sense... but... to be honest that's a really slow start for a really slow format. How about 'we have known each other long enough we've DECIDED to form a pack, so now we're getting serious' ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T01:20:13-07:00","id":468213,"title":"","content":"For all intensive purposes after the players all opt to post a flavor backround or state backround then I will move to the Teller's Action and set the first scene for everyone.<br /> <br /> In the mean time please feel free to post you're flavor or statistics, just make sure to end them with a (Narration End) bracket so I'll know that's all you intend to write or PM me so I'll know you're opting to wait until later on to flesh out your character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T03:21:08-07:00","id":468271,"title":"","content":"Okay I posted some background in the thread. Tried to edit it down, so I hope it isn't <i>too</i> long. I may or may not be very excited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T06:44:48-07:00","id":468363,"title":"","content":"I kind of like the flashback thing you did there. A little context might not be a bad thing just to get the writing juices flowing. I wonder how we can tie flashbacks towards Retias' first post? :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T06:50:27-07:00","id":468368,"title":"","content":"That was the state of affairs for Akule before joining the back. while I think Indiana's post has beaten mine out, she and he seem to have the same strife about feeling alone. Which is a nice tie to the inherent werewolf need for a pack, I think. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T19:20:03-07:00","id":469090,"title":"","content":"Way to go guys, especially Soonmot, great post man,I love how your handling the characters. I'll try to get something up here soon.<br /> <br /> If we want to go on with the first scene setting I'm ok with that, I plan on incorporating backstory through play, so no need to wait on that in the Ic unless you guys would like me to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1705,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","user":"Okami","date":". 04-05-2015, 12:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T23:12:09-07:00","id":469214,"title":"","content":"Edited my post to be more recent and show that Violet had already met Aliza and is taking her up on forming a pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5337-soonmot","name":"soonmot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5337_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T08:10:39-07:00","id":469344,"title":"","content":"Awesome. We now have a pattern of posting in 'descending' order, getting closer and closer to Retias' first post. Okami, if you want to write one 'yesterday' that's your character linking up with us, and then maybe we can also get some context from how/what Retias is doing right 'now', and then we'll be more-or-less ready to go, ST? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T19:49:32-07:00","id":469793,"title":"","content":"Excellent point Barbrarilen,<br /> <br /> For the first chapter of this Chronicle let's have this descending order be the posting order for everyone. During the next chapter I'll have another downtime and then it'll be a first come first serve for the next descending order. What do you all think? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T21:25:33-07:00","id":469852,"title":"","content":"Oh, for actual play (outside of combat) I thought it was just post when you have something to do/say otherwise conversations are going to be weird. I'm willing to try something different, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5337-soonmot","name":"soonmot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5337_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T22:12:40-07:00","id":469876,"title":"","content":"Ah, another good point. I totally forgot about that....<br /> <br /> Please ignore my last post. Keep up the good work everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T05:37:43-07:00","id":470061,"title":"","content":"I've seen it handled both ways, when there's a posting order it serves to allow other people to react to a conversation between two other characters or do something on the side, as post-as-you-can often causes a situation where some players cant get a word in edgewise. If they want the players can opt out of responding though, allowing the conversation to continue fluidly. However you guys want to do it is cool by me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T05:38:30-07:00","id":470062,"title":"","content":"I 